window.SITE_DATA = {"domains":[{"id":"molecular","zh":"分子生物學基礎","en":"Molecular Biology Foundations"},{"id":"sequencing","zh":"定序與變異分析","en":"Sequencing & Variant Analysis"},{"id":"transcriptomics","zh":"轉錄體學","en":"Transcriptomics"},{"id":"gwas","zh":"GWAS 與統計遺傳學","en":"GWAS & Statistical Genetics"},{"id":"prs","zh":"多基因風險分數","en":"Polygenic Risk Score"},{"id":"multiomics","zh":"多體學整合","en":"Multi-Omics Integration"},{"id":"precision","zh":"精準醫療","en":"Precision Medicine"}],"concepts":[{"id":"dna","zh":"去氧核糖核酸","en":"Deoxyribonucleic Acid","abbr":"DNA","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"DNA 就像一本用四個字母（A、C、G、T）寫成的說明書，記錄生物如何長成、如何運作。兩股 DNA 像拉鍊一樣扣在一起：A 一定對 T，C 一定對 G。","en":"DNA is like an instruction book written with four letters (A, C, G, T) describing how an organism is built and runs. Two strands zip together: A always pairs with T, and C with G."},"advanced":{"zh":"DNA 是由去氧核糖、磷酸骨架與四種含氮鹼基組成的雙股聚合物，兩股以互補鹼基配對（A–T、C–G）反向平行結合。互補性讓 DNA 能被複製，也讓定序與比對成為可能：讀到一股即可推得另一股。","en":"DNA is a double-stranded polymer of a deoxyribose–phosphate backbone and four nitrogenous bases; the antiparallel strands are held by complementary pairing (A–T, C–G). Complementarity enables replication and underlies sequencing and alignment: reading one strand determines the other."},"examples":{"zh":["序列 5'-ATGC-3' 的互補股是 3'-TACG-5'。"],"en":["The complement of 5'-ATGC-3' is 3'-TACG-5'."]},"related":["rna","chromosome","gene"]},{"id":"rna","zh":"核糖核酸","en":"Ribonucleic Acid","abbr":"RNA","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"如果 DNA 是存放在圖書館裡的原版說明書，RNA 就像拿出去用的影印本。RNA 通常只有一股，並用 U 取代 T。","en":"If DNA is the master copy kept in the library, RNA is the photocopy taken out to be used. RNA is usually single-stranded and uses U instead of T."},"advanced":{"zh":"RNA 以核糖為骨架、使用 A/U/C/G，多為單股。主要類型包括 mRNA（攜帶編碼訊息）、rRNA、tRNA，以及參與基因表現調控的 RNA。RNA-seq 測量的就是細胞中 RNA 的組成與量。","en":"RNA has a ribose backbone, uses A/U/C/G and is mostly single-stranded. Major types are mRNA (carrying coding information), rRNA, tRNA and regulatory RNAs. RNA-seq measures the composition and abundance of cellular RNA."},"examples":{"zh":["在編碼股（coding / sense strand）上的 ATG，對應到 mRNA 的 AUG。"],"en":["On the coding (sense) strand, ATG corresponds to AUG in the mRNA."]},"related":["dna","gene-expression","rna-seq"]},{"id":"chromosome","zh":"染色體","en":"Chromosome","abbr":"","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"整套 DNA 很長，所以被分成好幾「冊」包裝起來，每一冊就是一條染色體。人類細胞裡有 23 對、共 46 條。","en":"The whole DNA is very long, so it is packed into several \"volumes\" — each volume is a chromosome. Human cells have 23 pairs, 46 in total."},"advanced":{"zh":"每條染色體由一條連續的 DNA 分子與蛋白質組成。人類有 22 對體染色體（autosome）與一對性染色體（XX 或 XY）。基因體座標通常寫成「染色體:位置」，例如 chr1:12345。","en":"Each chromosome is one continuous DNA molecule packaged with proteins. Humans have 22 autosome pairs and one sex-chromosome pair (XX or XY). Genomic coordinates are written as chromosome:position, e.g. chr1:12345."},"examples":{"zh":["同一對染色體中，一條來自母親、一條來自父親。"],"en":["In each chromosome pair, one copy comes from the mother and one from the father."]},"related":["dna","locus","allele"]},{"id":"gene","zh":"基因","en":"Gene","abbr":"","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"基因是說明書裡的一個「章節」，通常負責製造一種蛋白質。人類大約有 2 萬個會做蛋白質的基因。","en":"A gene is a \"chapter\" of the instruction book, usually describing how to make one protein. Humans have about 20,000 protein-coding genes."},"advanced":{"zh":"基因是遺傳的基本單位，包含外顯子、內含子與調控序列。多數基因經轉錄與轉譯產生蛋白質，也有基因只產生功能性 RNA。蛋白質編碼基因的外顯子合起來就是 exome。","en":"The gene is the basic unit of inheritance, comprising exons, introns and regulatory sequence. Most genes are transcribed and translated into proteins; some yield only functional RNA. Exons of protein-coding genes together form the exome."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）若某基因的外顯子發生改變，可能改變其蛋白質產物；位於基因之間的變異則可能影響調控。"],"en":["(Illustrative) A change in a gene's exon may alter its protein product, while a variant between genes may affect regulation."]},"related":["locus","chromosome","wes","gene-expression"]},{"id":"locus","zh":"基因座","en":"Locus","abbr":"","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"Locus 就是「地址」：告訴你在哪一條染色體的哪個位置。基因是內容，locus 是位置。","en":"A locus is an \"address\": which chromosome and which position. A gene is content; a locus is a place."},"advanced":{"zh":"Locus 可以指單一鹼基位置，也可以指一段區域，例如一個基因或 GWAS 找到的關聯區段。GWAS 論文常說的「risk locus」是一個關聯區域，未必等於某一個基因。","en":"A locus can be a single base position or a region such as a gene or a GWAS association interval. A \"risk locus\" in a GWAS paper is an associated region, not necessarily a single gene."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）「chr1:1,000,000」是一個單鹼基 locus；「chr1:1,000,000–1,050,000」是一個區域 locus。"],"en":["(Illustrative) \"chr1:1,000,000\" is a single-base locus; \"chr1:1,000,000–1,050,000\" is a regional locus."]},"related":["gene","allele","snp","gwas"]},{"id":"allele","zh":"對偶基因","en":"Allele","abbr":"","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"同一個地址上可能有不同「版本」的字，例如有人是 A、有人是 G，這些版本就叫 allele。在體染色體上，每人在每個位置有兩份：一份來自爸爸、一份來自媽媽（男性 X 染色體上多數位置只有一份）。","en":"The same address can hold different \"versions\" — some people have A, others G. Those versions are alleles. On the autosomes everyone has two copies at each position, one from each parent (males carry one copy of most X-chromosome positions)."},"advanced":{"zh":"Allele 是某基因體位置上的序列版本，可以是單一鹼基或一段序列。兩份相同為 homozygous，不同為 heterozygous。在 GWAS/PRS 中需明確區分 reference allele、alternate allele 與 effect allele。","en":"An allele is a sequence version at a genomic position (single base or segment). Two identical copies = homozygous; different = heterozygous. GWAS/PRS work must distinguish reference, alternate and effect alleles."},"examples":{"zh":["某位置基因型為 A/G：此人帶有一個 A allele 和一個 G allele（heterozygous）。"],"en":["Genotype A/G at a site: one A allele and one G allele (heterozygous)."]},"related":["snp","genotype","effect-allele","allele-dosage"]},{"id":"snp","zh":"單核苷酸多型性","en":"Single Nucleotide Polymorphism","abbr":"SNP","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"SNP 是說明書中只差「一個字母」的地方。大部分 SNP 不影響健康，但有些會和疾病、藥物反應或身高等性狀有關。","en":"A SNP is a place where the instruction book differs by a single letter. Most SNPs do not affect health, but some are linked to disease, drug response or traits like height."},"advanced":{"zh":"SNP 是單一鹼基位置的變異，常以 rsID（dbSNP 編號）表示。GWAS 主要以 SNP 為檢定單位；由於 LD，被檢定的 SNP 常只是附近因果變異的標記（tag）。","en":"A SNP is a variant at a single base position, usually named by its dbSNP rsID. GWAS test mainly SNPs; because of LD, a tested SNP is often a tag for a nearby causal variant."},"examples":{"zh":["某 SNP 在多數人是 C，少數人是 T。"],"en":["At a given SNP most people carry C and a minority carry T."]},"related":["allele","genetic-variant","gwas","ld"]},{"id":"genetic-variant","zh":"遺傳變異","en":"Genetic Variant","abbr":"","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"任何和參考序列不一樣的地方都叫變異：可能是換一個字（SNV；在族群中常見的稱為 SNP）、少幾個字或多幾個字（indel），或是一大段被搬動（結構變異）。","en":"Any difference from the reference sequence is a variant: a swapped letter (an SNV; one that is common in a population is called an SNP), a few letters missing or added (indel), or a large rearranged segment (structural variant)."},"advanced":{"zh":"變異依大小與型態分為 SNV/SNP、indel 與 structural variant（含 CNV）。1000 Genomes Project 在 2,504 人中描述超過 8,800 萬個變異，說明人類變異極為豐富；其中大多數變異位點是罕見的，但單一個人基因體中的變異多數是常見變異。","en":"Variants are classified by size and form: SNV/SNP, indel, and structural variants (including CNVs). The 1000 Genomes Project described >88 million variants in 2,504 people, showing that human variation is abundant; most variant sites are rare, yet most variants in any one genome are common."},"examples":{"zh":["參考序列 ACGT，樣本序列 ACCT：第 3 個位置為 G→C 的 SNV。"],"en":["Reference ACGT, sample ACCT: a G→C SNV at position 3."]},"related":["snp","mutation","vcf","reference-genome"]},{"id":"genotype","zh":"基因型","en":"Genotype","abbr":"","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"基因型就是你在某個位置拿到的兩份版本組合，例如 A/A、A/G 或 G/G。它寫在 DNA 裡，不是肉眼看得到的特徵。","en":"Your genotype is the pair of versions you carry at a position, e.g. A/A, A/G or G/G. It is written in your DNA, not something you can see."},"advanced":{"zh":"Genotype 是對某 locus 變異類型的判定，可為硬判定（0/1/2）或 imputation 得到的機率性 dosage（0–2 的小數）。Genotype 只是 phenotype 的影響因素之一，必須和環境一起考慮。","en":"A genotype is the call of variant type at a locus — either a hard call (0/1/2) or a probabilistic imputed dosage (a decimal in 0–2). Genotype is only one influence on phenotype, alongside environment."},"examples":{"zh":["VCF 中的 0/1 代表一個 reference allele 加一個 alternate allele。"],"en":["0/1 in a VCF means one reference and one alternate allele."]},"related":["phenotype","allele","allele-dosage","vcf"]},{"id":"phenotype","zh":"表現型","en":"Phenotype","abbr":"","domain":"molecular","beginner":{"zh":"表現型是看得到或量得到的特徵，例如身高、血型或是否罹病。它受到基因和環境（飲食、運動、生活）一起影響。","en":"A phenotype is a trait you can see or measure — height, blood type, or having a disease. It is shaped by both genes and environment (diet, exercise, lifestyle)."},"advanced":{"zh":"Phenotype 可以是連續性狀（身高、LDL）或二元性狀（病例/對照），這會決定 GWAS 使用線性或邏輯斯迴歸，效應量也分別以 β 或 OR 表示。Genotype → Phenotype 不是決定論關係。","en":"Phenotypes can be quantitative (height, LDL) or binary (case/control), which determines linear vs logistic regression in GWAS and β vs OR as the effect size. Genotype → phenotype is not deterministic."},"examples":{"zh":["同卵雙胞胎基因型幾乎相同，但體重可能因生活型態而不同。"],"en":["Identical twins share nearly the same genotype but may differ in weight due to lifestyle."]},"related":["genotype","gwas","effect-size","genetic-risk"]},{"id":"ngs","zh":"次世代定序","en":"Next-Generation Sequencing","abbr":"NGS","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"NGS 就像把一本書剪成數百萬張小紙條，同時快速讀完，再用電腦拼回原書。它讓定序變得更快、更便宜。","en":"NGS is like cutting a book into millions of slips, reading them all at once, then reassembling the book by computer. It made sequencing faster and cheaper."},"advanced":{"zh":"NGS 泛指大規模平行定序。短讀段平台（數十至數百 bp）通量高、成本低；長讀段平台能跨越重複序列與結構變異，但（2016 年時）成本高、通量低。選擇平台取決於研究問題，而非一種技術取代全部。","en":"NGS denotes massively parallel sequencing. Short-read platforms (tens to hundreds of bp) give high throughput at low cost; long-read platforms span repeats and structural variants but were (as of 2016) costlier and lower-throughput. Platform choice follows the research question."},"examples":{"zh":["要找結構變異時，研究者可能選長讀段；大規模族群研究常選短讀段。"],"en":["To find structural variants a study may choose long reads; large population studies often choose short reads."]},"related":["wgs","wes","rna-seq","variant-calling"]},{"id":"wgs","zh":"全基因體定序","en":"Whole Genome Sequencing","abbr":"WGS","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"WGS 是把整本說明書從頭讀到尾，包括會做蛋白質的章節和其他所有部分。","en":"WGS reads the whole instruction book cover to cover — the protein-coding chapters and everything else."},"advanced":{"zh":"WGS 覆蓋編碼與非編碼區，可偵測 SNV、indel 與結構變異；覆蓋深度（coverage）影響偵測靈敏度。WGS、WES 與基因分型晶片常互補使用，例如 1000 Genomes Project 同時使用低覆蓋 WGS、深度 WES 與 array。","en":"WGS covers coding and non-coding regions and detects SNVs, indels and structural variants; coverage depth affects sensitivity. WGS, WES and genotyping arrays are often combined — the 1000 Genomes Project used low-coverage WGS, deep WES and arrays together."},"examples":{"zh":["30× 覆蓋度表示每個鹼基平均被讀到約 30 次。"],"en":["30× coverage means each base is read about 30 times on average."]},"related":["wes","ngs","reference-genome","variant-calling"]},{"id":"wes","zh":"全外顯子定序","en":"Whole Exome Sequencing","abbr":"WES","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"WES 只讀說明書中「真正寫製作方法」的段落（外顯子），大約只占全部的 1.5%，所以比較便宜。","en":"WES reads only the paragraphs that actually describe how to make proteins (exons) — about 1.5% of the whole book — so it costs less."},"advanced":{"zh":"WES 先以探針捕捉外顯子再定序，適合尋找影響蛋白質的變異；但會漏掉多數非編碼調控變異，且捕捉效率不均使覆蓋度較不平均。","en":"WES captures exons with probes before sequencing; it suits protein-altering variant discovery but misses most non-coding regulatory variants, and capture efficiency makes coverage less uniform."},"examples":{"zh":["疑似單基因遺傳疾病的診斷可能使用 WES 或 WGS（一般實務，依指引而異；本站未引用來源）。"],"en":["Diagnosis of a suspected monogenic disorder may use WES or WGS (general practice that varies by guideline; not sourced on this site)."]},"related":["wgs","gene","ngs"]},{"id":"reference-genome","zh":"參考基因體","en":"Reference Genome","abbr":"","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"參考基因體是一本「標準版」說明書。我們把每個人讀到的片段對照它，就能找出哪裡不一樣。","en":"A reference genome is a \"standard edition\" of the book. We compare each person's reads against it to find differences."},"advanced":{"zh":"參考基因體是比對與變異座標的基準。T2T-CHM13（2022）補上舊參考缺少的約 8%，包括著絲粒與近端著絲粒染色體短臂。參考只是座標系統，不代表「正常」或「理想」的人類序列。","en":"The reference genome is the coordinate system for alignment and variant calls. T2T-CHM13 (2022) filled the ~8% missing from earlier references, including centromeres and acrocentric short arms. A reference is a coordinate system, not a \"normal\" human sequence."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）變異 chr7:1,234,567 G>A 的座標依賴所用的參考版本。"],"en":["(Illustrative) The coordinate of a variant like chr7:1,234,567 G>A depends on the reference build used."]},"related":["wgs","variant-calling","genetic-variant"]},{"id":"variant-calling","zh":"變異偵測","en":"Variant Calling","abbr":"","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"把讀到的片段對回參考基因體後，電腦逐一檢查每個位置，判斷這個人是否帶有不同的版本，這就是 variant calling。","en":"After reads are aligned to the reference, software checks each position to decide whether the person carries a different version — that is variant calling."},"advanced":{"zh":"常見步驟（一般實務，本站未引用來源）：比對（alignment）→ 去除重複 → 鹼基品質校正 → 統計模型判定 genotype → 過濾。GATK 提供這類工具框架並用於 1000 Genomes 與 TCGA。Germline 與 somatic calling 的統計假設不同，後者需處理腫瘤純度與次克隆。","en":"Common steps (general practice, not sourced on this site): alignment → duplicate marking → base-quality recalibration → statistical genotype calling → filtering. GATK provides such a framework and was used in 1000 Genomes and TCGA. Germline and somatic calling differ: somatic calling must handle tumour purity and subclones."},"examples":{"zh":["某位置 30 條讀段中 15 條是 A、15 條是 G：可能是 heterozygous A/G。"],"en":["15 of 30 reads show A and 15 show G at a site: likely heterozygous A/G."]},"related":["vcf","ngs","mutation","reference-genome"]},{"id":"vcf","zh":"變異呼叫格式","en":"Variant Call Format","abbr":"VCF","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"VCF 是記錄「哪裡不一樣」的標準表格：哪條染色體、哪個位置、原本是什麼、變成什麼，以及每個人的基因型。","en":"VCF is the standard table of \"where it differs\": chromosome, position, reference, alternate, and each person's genotype."},"advanced":{"zh":"VCF 為文字格式，含 header（##）與固定欄位 CHROM, POS, ID, REF, ALT, QUAL, FILTER, INFO, FORMAT 及樣本欄；可存 SNP、indel 與結構變異，常以 bgzip 壓縮並以 tabix 建索引。","en":"VCF is a text format with header lines (##) and fixed columns CHROM, POS, ID, REF, ALT, QUAL, FILTER, INFO, FORMAT plus sample columns; it stores SNPs, indels and SVs and is usually bgzip-compressed and tabix-indexed."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）chr1  1000  demo1  A  G  …  GT  0|1 → 此人在該位置為 A/G"],"en":["(Illustrative) chr1  1000  demo1  A  G  …  GT  0|1 → this person is A/G at that site"]},"related":["variant-calling","genotype","genetic-variant"]},{"id":"mutation","zh":"突變（生殖細胞系 / 體細胞）","en":"Mutation (Germline / Somatic)","abbr":"","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"從爸媽遺傳來、身體每個細胞都有的變異叫 germline；出生後才在部分細胞中出現的（例如癌細胞）叫 somatic，不會傳給孩子。","en":"A variant inherited from parents and present in every cell is germline; one that arises later in some cells (e.g. cancer cells) is somatic and is not passed to children."},"advanced":{"zh":"Germline 變異存在於幾乎所有細胞，是 GWAS 與 PRS 的基礎；somatic 變異只存在部分細胞，是癌症基因體分析重點，常以腫瘤–正常配對樣本偵測。注意：Mutation 是 DNA 序列改變，基因表現（expression）是 RNA 量的改變，兩者不同。","en":"Germline variants are in virtually every cell and underlie GWAS and PRS; somatic variants are present in some cells only, central to cancer genomics, often detected with tumour–normal pairs. Note: a mutation is a DNA sequence change, whereas gene expression is RNA abundance."},"examples":{"zh":["腫瘤中出現、但同一人血液 DNA 中沒有的變異：somatic。"],"en":["A variant found in a tumour but not in the same person's blood DNA: somatic."]},"related":["genetic-variant","cancer-genomics","variant-classification","gene-expression"]},{"id":"variant-classification","zh":"變異致病性分類","en":"Variant Classification (ACMG/AMP)","abbr":"","domain":"sequencing","beginner":{"zh":"找到變異後，要判斷它是「會致病」、「不會致病」，還是「還不知道」。臨床上用五個等級來表示。","en":"After a variant is found, labs judge whether it causes disease, is harmless, or is still unknown, using five standard levels."},"advanced":{"zh":"ACMG/AMP（2015）五級：Pathogenic、Likely pathogenic、Uncertain significance（VUS）、Likely benign、Benign，依族群頻率、計算預測、功能與共分離等證據組合判定；適用於孟德爾疾病基因，不適用於 GWAS 的常見風險變異。","en":"ACMG/AMP (2015) five tiers — Pathogenic, Likely pathogenic, Uncertain significance (VUS), Likely benign, Benign — combining population, computational, functional and segregation evidence; designed for Mendelian disease genes, not common GWAS risk variants."},"examples":{"zh":["證據不足的變異標為 VUS，不應作為臨床決策依據。"],"en":["A variant with insufficient evidence is a VUS and should not drive clinical decisions."]},"related":["mutation","clinical-application"]},{"id":"gene-expression","zh":"基因表現","en":"Gene Expression","abbr":"","domain":"transcriptomics","beginner":{"zh":"每個細胞都有同一本說明書，但肝細胞和腦細胞「翻開來用」的章節不同。一個基因被讀取（轉錄成 RNA）的多寡，就是它的表現量。","en":"Every cell has the same book, but liver and brain cells open different chapters. How much a gene is read (transcribed into RNA) is its expression level."},"advanced":{"zh":"基因表現通常以 mRNA 豐度近似，會隨組織、時間與狀態改變。讀段數受轉錄本長度、定序深度與偏差影響，因此跨樣本比較前需要正規化。表現量改變不等於 DNA 突變：兩者分屬不同分子層次。","en":"Gene expression is usually approximated by mRNA abundance, which varies by tissue, time and state. Read counts depend on transcript length, depth and biases, so normalization precedes cross-sample comparison. Expression change is not DNA mutation: they are different molecular layers."},"examples":{"zh":["同一人的肝臟與腦組織，DNA 相同但表現譜不同。"],"en":["A person's liver and brain share DNA but have different expression profiles."]},"related":["rna","rna-seq","tpm","mutation"]},{"id":"rna-seq","zh":"RNA 定序","en":"RNA Sequencing","abbr":"RNA-seq","domain":"transcriptomics","beginner":{"zh":"RNA-seq 把細胞裡的 RNA 抓出來定序，數一數每個基因的「影印本」有幾份，就知道哪些基因正在忙。","en":"RNA-seq sequences the RNA in cells and counts the \"photocopies\" of each gene, revealing which genes are busy."},"advanced":{"zh":"流程：RNA 萃取 → 建庫（如 poly-A 選擇）→ 定序 → 品質控制 → 比對或 pseudo-alignment → 定量 → 差異表現／剪接／功能分析／eQTL。沒有一條流程適用所有研究；RNA-seq 也不是做完 WGS 才能做的下一步。","en":"Workflow: RNA extraction → library prep (e.g. poly-A selection) → sequencing → QC → alignment or pseudo-alignment → quantification → differential expression / splicing / functional analysis / eQTL. No single pipeline fits all studies, and RNA-seq is not a step that requires WGS first."},"examples":{"zh":["比較藥物處理前後的細胞，看哪些基因表現上升。"],"en":["Compare cells before and after drug treatment to see which genes go up."]},"related":["gene-expression","tpm","differential-expression","ngs"]},{"id":"tpm","zh":"每百萬轉錄本數","en":"Transcripts Per Million","abbr":"TPM","domain":"transcriptomics","beginner":{"zh":"長的基因天生會被讀到比較多次，TPM 先依長度校正，再換算成「每一百萬個轉錄本中占幾個」，讓同一樣本中的基因能互相比較。","en":"Longer genes naturally get more reads; TPM corrects for length then rescales to \"how many per million transcripts\", so genes within a sample can be compared."},"advanced":{"zh":"TPMᵢ = (cᵢ / ℓᵢ) / Σⱼ(cⱼ / ℓⱼ) × 10⁶，cᵢ 為讀段數、ℓᵢ 為有效長度。每個樣本 TPM 總和固定為 10⁶（Wagner 2012 對 RPKM 的修正）。相較 RPKM/FPKM，TPM 校正了轉錄本組成差異，被認為在樣本間較可比（C-TX-08）。限制：TPM 仍是相對量，若少數基因大量表現會壓縮其他基因數值；差異表現檢定應使用 count 模型（如 DESeq2）。","en":"TPMᵢ = (cᵢ / ℓᵢ) / Σⱼ(cⱼ / ℓⱼ) × 10⁶, with cᵢ read count and ℓᵢ effective length; each sample sums to 10⁶ (Wagner 2012's fix to RPKM). Compared with RPKM/FPKM, TPM normalizes for transcript composition and is considered more comparable between samples (C-TX-08). Limitation: TPM is still relative — a few very highly expressed genes compress the rest; differential testing should use count models (e.g. DESeq2)."},"examples":{"zh":["基因 A：100 讀段、長 1 kb；基因 B：100 讀段、長 2 kb → A 的 TPM 是 B 的兩倍。"],"en":["Gene A: 100 reads, 1 kb; gene B: 100 reads, 2 kb → A's TPM is twice B's."]},"related":["gene-expression","rna-seq","differential-expression"]},{"id":"expression-matrix","zh":"基因表現矩陣","en":"Gene Expression Matrix","abbr":"","domain":"transcriptomics","beginner":{"zh":"把結果整理成一張大表：每一列是一個基因、每一欄是一個樣本，格子裡是讀段數或表現量。","en":"Results are arranged in a big table: one row per gene, one column per sample, with counts or expression values in the cells."},"advanced":{"zh":"原始計數矩陣（genes × samples，非負整數）是 DESeq2 等差異分析的輸入；TPM 矩陣適合視覺化與樣本內比較。矩陣需搭配樣本資訊表（條件、批次）才能建模，並處理批次效應。","en":"A raw count matrix (genes × samples, non-negative integers) is the input to DESeq2-style differential analysis; TPM matrices suit visualization and within-sample comparison. A sample sheet (condition, batch) is required for modelling and batch correction."},"examples":{"zh":["20,000 個基因 × 12 個樣本 = 240,000 個數值。"],"en":["20,000 genes × 12 samples = 240,000 values."]},"related":["differential-expression","tpm","data-integration"]},{"id":"differential-expression","zh":"差異基因表現分析","en":"Differential Gene Expression","abbr":"DGE","domain":"transcriptomics","beginner":{"zh":"比較兩組（例如病人與健康者），找出哪些基因的表現量明顯不同。要有多個重複樣本，才能分辨真實差異與隨機波動。","en":"Compare two groups (e.g. patients vs healthy) to find genes whose expression clearly differs. Replicates are needed to tell real differences from noise."},"advanced":{"zh":"DESeq2 以負二項分布建模計數：Kᵢⱼ ~ NB(μᵢⱼ, αᵢ)，log₂ μᵢⱼ 以實驗設計線性建模；對 dispersion αᵢ 與 log₂ fold change 做 shrinkage 以穩定估計，再以多重檢定校正（如 Benjamini–Hochberg FDR）。","en":"DESeq2 models counts as Kᵢⱼ ~ NB(μᵢⱼ, αᵢ) with log₂ μᵢⱼ linear in the design; dispersions αᵢ and log₂ fold changes are shrunk for stability, followed by multiple-testing correction (e.g. Benjamini–Hochberg FDR)."},"examples":{"zh":["log₂FC = 1 代表表現量約為對照組的 2 倍。"],"en":["log₂FC = 1 means roughly 2× the control expression."]},"related":["expression-matrix","rna-seq","pathway-analysis","biomarker"]},{"id":"gwas","zh":"全基因體關聯研究","en":"Genome-Wide Association Study","abbr":"GWAS","domain":"gwas","beginner":{"zh":"GWAS 比較「有某疾病」和「沒有」的一大群人，在整個基因體裡找出在病人中比較常見的 SNP。找到的是「關聯」，不代表那個 SNP 就是病因：關聯不等於因果。","en":"GWAS compares large groups with and without a disease, scanning the whole genome for SNPs that are more common in patients. What it finds is association — not proof that the SNP causes the disease."},"advanced":{"zh":"對每個 SNP 以迴歸檢定 genotype dosage 與 phenotype 的關聯（連續性狀用線性迴歸、二元性狀用邏輯斯迴歸），並納入主成分等共變數校正族群分層。顯著 SNP 常透過 LD 標記附近未知的因果變異，需要 fine-mapping 與功能研究才能推論機制。","en":"Each SNP is tested by regressing phenotype on genotype dosage (linear for quantitative, logistic for binary traits), adjusting for covariates such as principal components to control population stratification. Significant SNPs often tag unknown causal variants via LD; fine-mapping and functional work are needed to infer mechanism."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）10,000 名病例與 10,000 名對照中，某 SNP 的 T allele 頻率分別為 32% 與 28%。"],"en":["(Illustrative) Among 10,000 cases and 10,000 controls, a SNP's T allele frequency is 32% vs 28%."]},"related":["snp","ld","p-value","effect-size","manhattan-plot","prs"]},{"id":"ld","zh":"連鎖不平衡","en":"Linkage Disequilibrium","abbr":"LD","domain":"gwas","beginner":{"zh":"距離很近的 SNP 常常「一起被遺傳」，像同一節車廂的乘客一起上下車。所以看到其中一個，就能猜到另一個。","en":"SNPs close together are often inherited together, like passengers in the same carriage. Seeing one lets you guess the other."},"advanced":{"zh":"LD 是不同基因座 allele 的非隨機關聯。常用 D = p_AB − p_A·p_B 與 r² = D² / [p_A(1−p_A)p_B(1−p_B)]。重組會隨世代打散 LD，且 LD 結構因族群歷史而異；這也是 GWAS 結果與 PRS 跨族群移植性受限的原因之一。","en":"LD is the nonrandom association of alleles at different loci, measured by D = p_AB − p_A·p_B and r² = D² / [p_A(1−p_A)p_B(1−p_B)]. Recombination erodes LD over generations, and LD patterns differ by population history — one reason GWAS hits and PRS transfer imperfectly across ancestries."},"examples":{"zh":["r² = 1：兩個 SNP 完全相關，檢定任一個的結果相同。"],"en":["r² = 1: two SNPs are perfectly correlated; testing either gives the same result."]},"related":["gwas","snp","prs-calculation","prs-portability"]},{"id":"effect-size","zh":"效應量（Beta / Odds Ratio）","en":"Effect Size (Beta / Odds Ratio)","abbr":"β / OR","domain":"gwas","beginner":{"zh":"效應量回答「每多一個風險版本，影響有多大」。量身高時用 β（多幾公分）；看是否得病時用 Odds Ratio（勝算多幾倍）。","en":"Effect size answers \"how much does each extra risk copy change things\". For height it is β (extra cm); for disease it is the odds ratio (how many times the odds)."},"advanced":{"zh":"連續性狀：β 為每增加一個 effect allele 的性狀平均變化。二元性狀：OR = e^β，β 為 logistic 迴歸係數，即 log(OR)。β 的正負號取決於所選的 effect allele；交換 effect/other allele 時 β 變號、OR 變倒數。","en":"Quantitative traits: β is the mean change per additional effect allele. Binary traits: OR = e^β where β is the logistic coefficient, i.e. log(OR). The sign of β depends on which allele is the effect allele; swapping alleles flips β's sign and inverts OR."},"examples":{"zh":["OR = 1.10 → β = ln(1.10) ≈ 0.095；換成另一個 allele 時 OR ≈ 0.91。"],"en":["OR = 1.10 → β = ln(1.10) ≈ 0.095; for the other allele OR ≈ 0.91."]},"related":["gwas","effect-allele","effect-weight","phenotype"]},{"id":"p-value","zh":"P 值與全基因體顯著性","en":"P-value & Genome-wide Significance","abbr":"","domain":"gwas","beginner":{"zh":"P 值表示「如果其實沒有關聯，看到這麼強結果的機率」。GWAS 一次檢查上百萬個 SNP，很容易碰巧中獎，所以門檻非常嚴格：p < 0.00000005。","en":"A p-value is the chance of seeing a result this strong if there were truly no association. GWAS test millions of SNPs, so lucky hits are common — hence the strict threshold p < 0.00000005."},"advanced":{"zh":"全基因體顯著閾值 5 × 10⁻⁸ 大致相當於對約一百萬個獨立檢定做 Bonferroni 校正（0.05 / 10⁶）。P 值小只代表統計證據強，不代表效應大，也不代表因果；效應量要另外看 β 或 OR。","en":"The 5 × 10⁻⁸ genome-wide threshold roughly corresponds to a Bonferroni correction for ~one million independent tests (0.05 / 10⁶). A small p-value means strong statistical evidence, not a large effect and not causation; look at β or OR for magnitude."},"examples":{"zh":["p = 3 × 10⁻⁹ 達全基因體顯著；p = 2 × 10⁻⁶ 則只是「提示性」關聯。"],"en":["p = 3 × 10⁻⁹ is genome-wide significant; p = 2 × 10⁻⁶ is only suggestive."]},"related":["gwas","manhattan-plot","effect-size"]},{"id":"manhattan-plot","zh":"曼哈頓圖","en":"Manhattan Plot","abbr":"","domain":"gwas","beginner":{"zh":"曼哈頓圖是呈現 GWAS 結果的圖：每個點是一個 SNP，左右位置是它在染色體上的位置，越高代表關聯越強；圖上的橫線就是全基因體顯著門檻 5 × 10⁻⁸。因為一根根柱子像曼哈頓的天際線而得名。","en":"A Manhattan plot displays GWAS results: each dot is a SNP, placed left to right by its position on the chromosomes and higher for stronger association; the horizontal line marks the 5 × 10⁻⁸ genome-wide threshold."},"advanced":{"zh":"x 軸：SNP 依基因體位置排列（依染色體分段）；y 軸：−log₁₀(P)，例如 P = 10⁻⁸ 對應 8。顯著閾值線對應 P = 5 × 10⁻⁸（−log₁₀ ≈ 7.3）。常與 Q–Q plot 一起檢查檢定統計是否膨脹（C-GW-09）。","en":"x-axis: SNPs ordered by genomic position (grouped by chromosome); y-axis: −log10(P), e.g. P = 10⁻⁸ plots at 8. The threshold line is P = 5 × 10⁻⁸ (−log10 ≈ 7.3). It is usually read together with a Q–Q plot to check for inflated test statistics (C-GW-09)."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）在簡報中的模擬 GWAS 圖上，超過門檻線的點代表達到全基因體顯著。"],"en":["(Illustrative) On the simulated GWAS figure in the slides, points above the line are genome-wide significant."]},"related":["gwas","p-value"]},{"id":"gwas-catalog","zh":"GWAS Catalog","en":"NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog","abbr":"","domain":"gwas","beginner":{"zh":"GWAS Catalog 是一個公開的「關聯結果圖書館」，把已發表 GWAS 找到的 SNP–性狀關聯整理起來，任何人都能查。","en":"The GWAS Catalog is a public \"library\" of SNP–trait associations from published GWAS that anyone can search."},"advanced":{"zh":"由 NHGRI 與 EMBL-EBI 維護，提供人工整理的關聯、summary statistics 與標準化性狀註解，並連結 PGS Catalog。研究者用它取得 PRS 權重來源或比較前人結果。","en":"Maintained by NHGRI and EMBL-EBI, it provides curated associations, summary statistics and standardized trait annotation, linked to the PGS Catalog. Researchers use it to source PRS weights or compare prior findings."},"examples":{"zh":["查詢某性狀，即可看到相關 SNP、效應量、P 值與研究族群。"],"en":["Search a trait to see associated SNPs, effect sizes, p-values and study populations."]},"related":["gwas","pgs-catalog","effect-weight"]},{"id":"gwas-diversity","zh":"研究族群多樣性","en":"Population Diversity in GWAS","abbr":"","domain":"gwas","beginner":{"zh":"過去大部分 GWAS 的參與者是歐洲血統。只用某一群人找到的結果，套用到其他族群時不一定準確。","en":"Most past GWAS participants were of European ancestry. Results from one group may not hold as well in others."},"advanced":{"zh":"Popejoy & Fullerton（2016）：2009 年 96% 為歐洲血統，2016 年非歐洲約 20%，但非洲、拉丁美洲血統、西語裔與原住民族群合計 <4%。族群間 allele 頻率與 LD 結構不同，造成發現偏差與 PRS 移植性下降。","en":"Popejoy & Fullerton (2016): 96% European in 2009; ~20% non-European by 2016, but African and Latin American ancestry, Hispanic and indigenous groups together <4%. Differences in allele frequencies and LD cause discovery bias and reduced PRS portability."},"examples":{"zh":["某 SNP 在一族群常見、在另一族群罕見，其可檢測性就不同。"],"en":["A SNP common in one population but rare in another has different detectability."]},"related":["gwas","prs-portability","ethics-equity","ld"]},{"id":"prs","zh":"多基因風險分數","en":"Polygenic Risk Score","abbr":"PRS","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"很多疾病不是單一基因造成，而是成千上萬個小影響累加。PRS 把一個人帶有的風險版本「加權加總」成一個分數，用來和其他人比較高低；它是相對位置，不是你一定會不會得病的答案。","en":"Many diseases come from thousands of small effects added together. A PRS adds up a person's risk versions, weighted, into one score for comparison with others; it is a relative position, not a yes/no answer about getting the disease."},"advanced":{"zh":"PRS 估計個體的遺傳傾向（genetic liability），通常只解釋性狀變異的一小部分。其表現依賴 GWAS 樣本量、目標族群與 base 族群的相似度，以及 LD 處理方式。個人與臨床效用仍有爭議；目前證據主要支持群體層級的風險分層。","en":"A PRS estimates genetic liability and typically explains a small fraction of trait variance. Performance depends on GWAS sample size, similarity between base and target populations, and LD handling. Personal and clinical utility is debated; evidence mainly supports group-level stratification."},"examples":{"zh":["（模擬）某人 PRS 落在第 90 百分位：表示在同一參考族群中高於 90% 的人，並非 90% 機率罹病。"],"en":["(Simulated) A PRS at the 90th percentile means higher than 90% of the reference population — not a 90% chance of disease."]},"related":["prs-calculation","effect-weight","allele-dosage","prs-portability","gwas"]},{"id":"effect-allele","zh":"效應對偶基因","en":"Effect Allele","abbr":"","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"GWAS 會指定一個版本作為「被計算的那個」，叫 effect allele。效應量描述的就是每多帶一個 effect allele 的影響。","en":"A GWAS designates one version as the counted one — the effect allele. The effect size describes the impact of each extra copy of it."},"advanced":{"zh":"Effect allele 不一定是 alternate allele 或少見 allele，也不一定增加風險（β 可為負）。合併 GWAS 與目標 genotype 時必須對齊 allele（含 strand flip 與 palindromic SNP 如 A/T、C/G），否則權重符號會錯。","en":"The effect allele is not necessarily the alternate or minor allele, nor necessarily risk-increasing (β can be negative). When combining GWAS with target genotypes, alleles must be harmonized (strand flips, palindromic A/T, C/G SNPs) or weights get the wrong sign."},"examples":{"zh":["GWAS：effect allele = G、β = +0.1；某人為 A/G → dosage = 1。"],"en":["GWAS: effect allele G, β = +0.1; a person with A/G → dosage 1."]},"related":["allele","allele-dosage","effect-size","effect-weight"]},{"id":"allele-dosage","zh":"對偶基因劑量","en":"Allele Dosage","abbr":"G","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"Dosage 就是「數一數你有幾個 effect allele」：0 個、1 個或 2 個。","en":"Dosage means counting your effect alleles: 0, 1 or 2."},"advanced":{"zh":"硬判定 dosage ∈ {0,1,2}；imputation 給出期望劑量 E[G] = P(heterozygous) + 2·P(homozygous for the effect allele)，為 0–2 的小數。例如 P(heterozygous)=0.4、P(effect allele 同型合子)=0.5 → dosage = 1.4。","en":"Hard-called dosage ∈ {0,1,2}; imputation yields expected dosage E[G] = P(heterozygous) + 2·P(homozygous for the effect allele), a decimal in 0–2. E.g. P(heterozygous)=0.4, P(homozygous effect)=0.5 → dosage 1.4."},"examples":{"zh":["effect allele = G：A/A → 0，A/G → 1，G/G → 2。"],"en":["Effect allele G: A/A → 0, A/G → 1, G/G → 2."]},"related":["effect-allele","genotype","prs-calculation"]},{"id":"effect-weight","zh":"效應權重","en":"Effect Weight","abbr":"β","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"每個 SNP 的影響大小不同，權重就是「這一票值幾分」，通常直接取自 GWAS 的效應量。","en":"Each SNP matters by a different amount; the weight is how much its vote counts, usually taken from the GWAS effect size."},"advanced":{"zh":"權重來自 GWAS summary statistics 的 β 或 log(OR)（或 Z 分數）。C+T 直接使用邊際 β；LDpred、lassosum 等方法以 LD 與先驗分布（或 LASSO 型懲罰）收縮 summary statistics 的權重；以個體層級基因型聯合擬合的 BLUP、LASSO 預測則是另一類方法。權重應取自與目標樣本不重疊的 GWAS。","en":"Weights come from GWAS summary statistics: β or log(OR) (or Z-scores). C+T uses marginal β directly; LDpred, lassosum and similar methods shrink summary-statistic weights using LD and priors (or LASSO-type penalties); BLUP or LASSO models fitted jointly on individual-level genotypes are a separate class. Weights must come from a GWAS that does not overlap the target sample."},"examples":{"zh":["OR = 1.2 → 權重 β = ln 1.2 ≈ 0.182。"],"en":["OR = 1.2 → weight β = ln 1.2 ≈ 0.182."]},"related":["effect-size","prs-calculation","gwas-catalog","pgs-catalog"]},{"id":"prs-calculation","zh":"PRS 計算","en":"PRS Calculation","abbr":"","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"計算方法很簡單：每個 SNP 的「權重 × 你有幾個」，全部加起來。PRS = Σ(βᵢ × Gᵢ)。","en":"The calculation is simple: for each SNP, weight × how many copies you have, then add them up. PRS = Σ(βᵢ × Gᵢ)."},"advanced":{"zh":"PRSⱼ = Σᵢ βᵢ · Gᵢⱼ。實務步驟：base GWAS 與 target 資料 QC → allele 對齊 → 處理 LD（clumping 或 LD-aware 收縮）→ 選擇 SNP 集合（P 值門檻或全基因體）→ 計算 → 在獨立樣本評估。分數常再標準化為 z-score 或百分位。","en":"PRSⱼ = Σᵢ βᵢ · Gᵢⱼ. Practical steps: QC base GWAS and target data → harmonize alleles → handle LD (clumping or LD-aware shrinkage) → choose SNP set (P threshold or genome-wide) → compute → evaluate in an independent sample. Scores are often standardized to z-scores or percentiles."},"examples":{"zh":["（模擬）β = (0.12, −0.08)、G = (2, 1) → PRS = 0.24 − 0.08 = 0.16。"],"en":["(Simulated) β = (0.12, −0.08), G = (2, 1) → PRS = 0.24 − 0.08 = 0.16."]},"related":["prs","effect-weight","allele-dosage","ld","prs-validation"]},{"id":"prs-validation","zh":"PRS 驗證","en":"PRS Validation","abbr":"","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"做好的分數要拿到「沒看過的新一群人」測試，看看高分的人是不是真的比較常得病。用同一群人自己考自己，會高估效果。","en":"A score must be tested on new people it has never seen, to check that high scorers really get the disease more often. Testing on the same people overstates performance."},"advanced":{"zh":"常見指標：AUC、R²（liability scale）、高低百分位的 OR。base 與 target 樣本不可重疊，也應移除近親。Khera 2018 在 UK Biobank 以 Phase I 選分數、Phase II 獨立測試，但兩者皆為英國血統，結果不能直接外推到其他族群。","en":"Common metrics: AUC, liability-scale R², OR between top and bottom percentiles. Base and target samples must not overlap and close relatives should be removed. Khera 2018 selected scores in UK Biobank Phase I and tested in Phase II, but both were British-ancestry, so results do not transfer directly to other ancestries."},"examples":{"zh":["AUC = 0.5 代表跟擲硬幣一樣；越接近 1 區分能力越好。"],"en":["AUC = 0.5 is coin-flip; closer to 1 means better discrimination."]},"related":["prs","prs-portability","prs-calculation","disease-prediction"]},{"id":"prs-portability","zh":"PRS 跨族群適用性","en":"PRS Portability Across Ancestries","abbr":"","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"如果分數主要用歐洲族群的資料做出來，用在亞洲或非洲族群時就常常沒那麼準。","en":"If a score is built mostly from European data, it is often less accurate in Asian or African populations."},"advanced":{"zh":"Martin 等人（2019）指出目前 PRS 在歐洲血統中準確度高出數倍，源自 GWAS 的歐洲偏重；原因包括 allele 頻率差異、LD 結構差異與標記 SNP 不同。對策：多元族群 GWAS、跨族群方法，並公開 summary statistics。","en":"Martin et al. (2019) showed current PRSs are several-fold more accurate in European ancestry because GWAS are Eurocentric; causes include allele-frequency and LD differences and differing tag SNPs. Remedies: diverse GWAS, multi-ancestry methods, public summary statistics."},"examples":{"zh":["同一分數在兩族群的 R² 可能相差數倍。"],"en":["The same score's R² can differ several-fold between two populations."]},"related":["prs","gwas-diversity","ld","ethics-equity"]},{"id":"pgs-catalog","zh":"PGS Catalog","en":"Polygenic Score Catalog","abbr":"PGS","domain":"prs","beginner":{"zh":"PGS Catalog 是公開的「分數食譜庫」：每個已發表的 PRS 用了哪些 SNP、哪個 allele、多少權重，都可以下載。","en":"The PGS Catalog is a public \"recipe library\" of published scores: which SNPs, which alleles and what weights, all downloadable."},"advanced":{"zh":"提供評分檔（variant、effect allele、weight）與標準化 metadata（開發族群、評估族群、效能指標），支援再現與獨立評估。選用分數時應檢查其開發與評估族群是否符合目標族群。","en":"It provides scoring files (variant, effect allele, weight) and standardized metadata (development and evaluation ancestry, performance metrics) for reproducibility. When choosing a score, check that its development and evaluation populations match the target."},"examples":{"zh":["每個分數有 PGS 編號（如 PGS000001 格式）。"],"en":["Each score has an ID in the format PGS000001."]},"related":["prs","gwas-catalog","effect-weight"]},{"id":"multi-omics","zh":"多體學","en":"Multi-Omics","abbr":"","domain":"multiomics","beginner":{"zh":"只看 DNA 就像只看食譜，只看 RNA 像只看廚房正在煮什麼。多體學把食譜、正在煮的菜、端上桌的成品一起看，更容易了解問題出在哪裡。","en":"Looking only at DNA is like reading the recipe; looking only at RNA is seeing what is cooking. Multi-omics looks at the recipe, the cooking and the served dish together to find where things go wrong."},"advanced":{"zh":"多體學整合基因體、轉錄體、表觀基因體、蛋白體、代謝體等層次，目標是追蹤疾病背後的資訊流動，而不是單一層次的關聯。它不是 WGS → RNA-seq → GWAS 的固定流程；研究可從任何層次出發。","en":"Multi-omics integrates genome, transcriptome, epigenome, proteome, metabolome and other layers to follow the flow of information underlying disease, beyond single-layer associations. It is not a fixed WGS → RNA-seq → GWAS pipeline; studies may start from any layer."},"examples":{"zh":["同一批腫瘤同時有突變、表現與甲基化資料，可交互比對。"],"en":["The same tumours with mutation, expression and methylation data can be cross-compared."]},"related":["genomics","gene-expression","data-integration","cancer-genomics"]},{"id":"genomics","zh":"基因體學","en":"Genomics","abbr":"","domain":"multiomics","beginner":{"zh":"基因體學研究「整本說明書」，而不是一次只看一個基因。GWAS、WGS 都屬於基因體學工具。","en":"Genomics studies the whole instruction book rather than one gene at a time. GWAS and WGS are genomics tools."},"advanced":{"zh":"基因體學涵蓋序列、變異與結構分析。基因分型晶片帶來大規模 GWAS，加上全轉錄本測量，催生了 integrative genetics；之後蛋白體學、代謝體學等其他體學也常被納入。基因體層次的資料多為一生大致固定的 germline 變異（癌症中的 somatic 變異除外）。","en":"Genomics covers sequence, variation and structure. Genotyping arrays enabled large GWAS and, with transcriptome-wide measurement, gave rise to integrative genetics; other omics such as proteomics and metabolomics are now often incorporated too. Genome-level data are mostly germline variants fixed over life (except somatic variants in cancer)."},"examples":{"zh":["用 WGS 比較一家人的變異以找出遺傳疾病原因。"],"en":["Using WGS to compare variants across a family to find a hereditary cause."]},"related":["multi-omics","wgs","gwas","mutation"]},{"id":"data-integration","zh":"資料整合","en":"Data Integration","abbr":"","domain":"multiomics","beginner":{"zh":"把 DNA 變異和 RNA 表現量放在一起看：例如某個變異是不是讓附近基因的表現變高或變低。","en":"Put DNA variants and RNA expression side by side: for example, does a variant make a nearby gene's expression go up or down?"},"advanced":{"zh":"整合策略可分為 genome first（從 GWAS locus 出發找機制）、phenotype first 與 environment first。典型例子是 eQTL mapping：以 genotype 預測表現量 (expression ~ dosage)。挑戰包括樣本對應、批次效應、不同資料尺度與缺失值。","en":"Strategies include genome-first (from a GWAS locus toward mechanism), phenotype-first and environment-first. A typical example is eQTL mapping: expression ~ dosage. Challenges include sample matching, batch effects, differing data scales and missing values."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）帶 G/G 的人某基因表現量平均高於 A/A：該 SNP 可能是 eQTL。"],"en":["(Illustrative) G/G carriers express a gene more than A/A carriers on average: the SNP may be an eQTL."]},"related":["multi-omics","expression-matrix","gwas","mutation"]},{"id":"pathway-analysis","zh":"路徑分析","en":"Pathway Analysis","abbr":"","domain":"multiomics","beginner":{"zh":"一次看到幾百個差異基因很難理解。路徑分析問的是：這些基因是不是集中在某些生物功能（例如發炎、細胞分裂）？","en":"Hundreds of differential genes are hard to interpret. Pathway analysis asks whether they cluster in certain biological functions such as inflammation or cell division."},"advanced":{"zh":"方法包括過度表現分析（超幾何檢定）與 Gene Set Enrichment Analysis（依排序檢定基因集合是否集中於一端）。結果依賴所選基因集合資料庫與背景基因，需多重檢定校正。","en":"Methods include over-representation analysis (hypergeometric test) and Gene Set Enrichment Analysis (testing whether a gene set concentrates at one end of a ranked list). Results depend on the gene-set database and background, and need multiple-testing correction."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）差異基因中有大量細胞週期相關基因 → 提示細胞增生改變。"],"en":["(Illustrative) Many cell-cycle genes among DE genes → suggests altered proliferation."]},"related":["differential-expression","biomarker","multi-omics"]},{"id":"biomarker","zh":"生物標記","en":"Biomarker","abbr":"","domain":"multiomics","beginner":{"zh":"生物標記是可以測量、能反映身體狀態的指標，例如某個突變或某個基因的表現量，可能幫助判斷疾病類型或治療選擇。","en":"A biomarker is a measurable indicator of body state — such as a mutation or a gene's expression level — that may help classify disease or choose treatment."},"advanced":{"zh":"分子生物標記可為 DNA（突變）、RNA（表現特徵）、蛋白或代謝物。從研究發現到臨床使用需經分析效度、臨床效度與臨床效用驗證（一般框架，本站未引用來源）。TCGA Pan-Cancer 的目標之一是依基因體特徵跨癌種延伸療法，這屬研究目標，非已證實結果。","en":"Molecular biomarkers can be DNA (mutations), RNA (expression signatures), proteins or metabolites. Moving from discovery to clinic requires analytical validity, clinical validity and clinical utility (a general framework, not sourced on this site). Extending therapies across cancers by genomic profile is a TCGA Pan-Cancer aim, not a demonstrated result."},"examples":{"zh":["（示意）某腫瘤帶有特定突變時，可能適用針對該突變的標靶藥物。"],"en":["(Illustrative) A tumour with a specific mutation may be eligible for a drug targeting it."]},"related":["cancer-genomics","pathway-analysis","clinical-application","differential-expression"]},{"id":"precision-medicine","zh":"精準醫療","en":"Precision Medicine","abbr":"","domain":"precision","beginner":{"zh":"傳統醫療常以「平均的病人」設計治療；精準醫療則考慮每個人在基因、環境與生活型態的差異，找出更適合的預防與治療方式。","en":"Traditional care is often designed for the \"average patient\"; precision medicine considers each person's genes, environment and lifestyle to choose better prevention and treatment."},"advanced":{"zh":"美國 Precision Medicine Initiative（2015）近期以癌症為重點，長期擴及所有疾病。基因資訊只是其中一部分，必須與臨床資料、環境暴露和生活型態整合；並非所有基因檢測結果都能改變臨床決策。","en":"The US Precision Medicine Initiative (2015) focused near-term on cancer and long-term on all disease. Genetic information is one component, integrated with clinical data, environment and lifestyle; not every genetic result changes clinical decisions."},"examples":{"zh":["依腫瘤的分子特徵選擇治療，而非只看腫瘤長在哪個器官。"],"en":["Choosing therapy by a tumour's molecular profile, not only by the organ it arose in."]},"related":["genetic-risk","cancer-genomics","clinical-application","multi-omics"]},{"id":"genetic-risk","zh":"遺傳風險：相對與絕對","en":"Genetic Risk: Relative vs Absolute","abbr":"","domain":"precision","beginner":{"zh":"「風險高三倍」聽起來很可怕，但如果原本機率是 1%，三倍也只是 3%。相對風險不等於絕對風險；而且基因之外，環境與生活也很重要。","en":"\"Three times the risk\" sounds scary, but if the baseline is 1%, three times is 3%. Relative risk is not absolute risk — and environment and lifestyle matter beyond genes."},"advanced":{"zh":"PRS 研究常以「前 x% 與其餘人口比較」的勝算比（OR）或相對風險呈現。絕對風險 = 比較組的風險 × 相對風險；若研究報告的是 OR，只有在結果罕見時 OR 才近似相對風險。估計絕對風險需要目標族群的年齡、性別別發生率。Khera 等人指出，未來需考慮如何同時評估並溝通絕對與相對風險。","en":"PRS studies often present an odds ratio or relative risk for the top x% versus the rest. Absolute risk = risk in the comparison group × relative risk; when a study reports an OR, OR ≈ RR only for rare outcomes. Estimating absolute risk needs age- and sex-specific incidence in the target population. Khera et al. note it will be important to consider how to assess and communicate both absolute and relative risks."},"examples":{"zh":["（模擬）比較組 10 年風險 2%、相對風險 1.5 → 絕對風險 2% × 1.5 = 3%。"],"en":["(Simulated) Comparison-group 10-year risk 2%, relative risk 1.5 → absolute risk 2% × 1.5 = 3%."]},"related":["prs","disease-prediction","phenotype"]},{"id":"disease-prediction","zh":"疾病風險預測","en":"Disease Prediction","abbr":"","domain":"precision","beginner":{"zh":"預測是「估計機率」，不是「判決」。高風險的人不一定會生病，低風險的人也可能生病。預測結果要交由醫師結合其他資訊判讀。","en":"Prediction estimates probability; it is not a verdict. High-risk people may stay well and low-risk people may get sick. Results should be interpreted by clinicians with other information."},"advanced":{"zh":"Khera 2018 主張可考慮將 PRS 納入臨床（冠狀動脈疾病高 PRS 族群的盛行率為同等風險單基因突變攜帶者的 20 倍），但這是英國血統單一世代的結果；Martin 2019 則警告跨族群準確度不一。PRS 引導篩檢是否改善臨床結果，目前本系統尚無可驗證證據（Pending）。","en":"Khera 2018 proposed considering PRS in clinical care (high-PRS prevalence 20× that of monogenic carriers with comparable CAD risk), but in a single British-ancestry cohort; Martin 2019 warns of uneven accuracy across ancestries. Whether PRS-guided screening improves outcomes has no verified evidence in this system (Pending)."},"examples":{"zh":["研究會評估「把 PRS 加進年齡、血壓、膽固醇等臨床因子」是否改善預測；本站沒有已驗證的來源說明改善幅度。"],"en":["Studies evaluate whether adding a PRS to clinical factors such as age, blood pressure and cholesterol improves prediction; this site has no verified source on the size of that gain."]},"related":["genetic-risk","prs-validation","prs-portability","clinical-application"]},{"id":"cancer-genomics","zh":"癌症基因體學","en":"Cancer Genomics","abbr":"","domain":"precision","beginner":{"zh":"癌症是細胞的 DNA 出現後天變化而失控生長。分析腫瘤的突變、RNA 與其他分子資料，可以了解癌症類型並尋找治療方向。","en":"Cancer arises when acquired DNA changes make cells grow out of control. Analysing a tumour's mutations, RNA and other molecules helps classify it and find treatment options."},"advanced":{"zh":"TCGA 在 DNA、RNA、蛋白質與表觀遺傳層次分析大量腫瘤；Pan-Cancer 比較 12 種腫瘤類型的共通性與差異。癌症基因體以 somatic 變異為主，需配對正常組織區分 germline 背景。","en":"TCGA profiled many tumours at DNA, RNA, protein and epigenetic levels; Pan-Cancer compared commonalities and differences across 12 tumour types. Cancer genomics focuses on somatic variants, using matched normal tissue to separate germline background."},"examples":{"zh":["腫瘤–正常配對定序：只在腫瘤出現的變異視為 somatic。"],"en":["Tumour–normal paired sequencing: variants present only in the tumour are somatic."]},"related":["mutation","multi-omics","biomarker","precision-medicine"]},{"id":"clinical-application","zh":"臨床應用","en":"Clinical Application","abbr":"","domain":"precision","beginner":{"zh":"研究上的發現要用在病人身上，需要合格實驗室檢測、專業人員判讀，以及清楚的風險溝通。這個網站是教材，不是診斷工具。","en":"Using research findings for patients requires certified labs, expert interpretation and clear risk communication. This website is teaching material, not a diagnostic tool."},"advanced":{"zh":"ACMG 建議臨床分子遺傳檢測於 CLIA 認證實驗室進行，由具認證的專家判讀，並以五級分類描述孟德爾疾病變異。研究級 PRS 與臨床檢測之間仍需驗證效度、效用、族群適用性與倫理規範。","en":"ACMG recommends clinical molecular genetic testing in CLIA-approved labs with board-certified interpretation and five-tier classification for Mendelian variants. Research-grade PRS still needs validity, utility, population applicability and ethical safeguards before clinical use."},"examples":{"zh":["消費者基因檢測的結果，不能直接當作臨床診斷。"],"en":["Direct-to-consumer genetic results are not a clinical diagnosis."]},"related":["variant-classification","precision-medicine","ethics-equity","disease-prediction"]},{"id":"ethics-equity","zh":"倫理、隱私與公平性","en":"Ethics, Privacy & Equity","abbr":"","domain":"precision","beginner":{"zh":"基因資料可以辨識個人、也牽涉家人，必須保護隱私。若研究只包含少數族群，工具可能對其他人比較不準，造成不公平。","en":"Genetic data can identify a person and implicates relatives, so privacy must be protected. If research includes only some groups, tools may be less accurate for others, creating inequity."},"advanced":{"zh":"Martin 2019 主張公平的 PRS 需要提升研究族群多樣性並公開 summary statistics；Popejoy 2016 記錄 GWAS 族群組成偏差。其他議題包括知情同意、資料再識別風險、結果回饋與歧視風險。","en":"Martin 2019 argues equitable PRS requires diverse cohorts and public summary statistics; Popejoy 2016 documents the skewed ancestry of GWAS. Other issues include informed consent, re-identification risk, return of results and discrimination."},"examples":{"zh":["本專案只使用模擬基因型，不收集任何個人資料。"],"en":["This project uses only simulated genotypes and collects no personal data."]},"related":["prs-portability","gwas-diversity","clinical-application"]}],"relations":[{"from":"dna","to":"chromosome","label":"packaged into"},{"from":"dna","to":"rna","label":"transcribed into"},{"from":"chromosome","to":"gene","label":"contains"},{"from":"gene","to":"locus","label":"located at"},{"from":"locus","to":"allele","label":"has versions"},{"from":"snp","to":"allele","label":"has alleles"},{"from":"snp","to":"genetic-variant","label":"is a type of"},{"from":"allele","to":"genotype","label":"pair forms"},{"from":"genotype","to":"phenotype","label":"contributes to (with environment)"},{"from":"ngs","to":"wgs","label":"enables"},{"from":"ngs","to":"wes","label":"enables"},{"from":"ngs","to":"rna-seq","label":"enables"},{"from":"wgs","to":"variant-calling","label":"input to"},{"from":"wes","to":"variant-calling","label":"input to"},{"from":"reference-genome","to":"variant-calling","label":"coordinate system for"},{"from":"variant-calling","to":"vcf","label":"outputs"},{"from":"mutation","to":"genomics","label":"studied by"},{"from":"mutation","to":"variant-classification","label":"interpreted by"},{"from":"rna-seq","to":"gene-expression","label":"measures"},{"from":"rna-seq","to":"expression-matrix","label":"produces"},{"from":"expression-matrix","to":"tpm","label":"normalized as"},{"from":"expression-matrix","to":"differential-expression","label":"input to"},{"from":"differential-expression","to":"pathway-analysis","label":"interpreted by"},{"from":"snp","to":"gwas","label":"tested in"},{"from":"gwas","to":"effect-size","label":"estimates"},{"from":"gwas","to":"p-value","label":"reports"},{"from":"p-value","to":"manhattan-plot","label":"visualized in"},{"from":"ld","to":"gwas","label":"explains tagging in"},{"from":"gwas","to":"gwas-catalog","label":"curated in"},{"from":"gwas-diversity","to":"prs-portability","label":"limits"},{"from":"effect-size","to":"effect-weight","label":"becomes"},{"from":"effect-size","to":"prs","label":"weights"},{"from":"effect-allele","to":"allele-dosage","label":"counted as"},{"from":"allele-dosage","to":"prs-calculation","label":"G in Σβ·G"},{"from":"effect-weight","to":"prs-calculation","label":"β in Σβ·G"},{"from":"prs-calculation","to":"prs","label":"produces"},{"from":"prs","to":"prs-validation","label":"evaluated by"},{"from":"pgs-catalog","to":"prs","label":"distributes"},{"from":"genomics","to":"multi-omics","label":"layer of"},{"from":"gene-expression","to":"multi-omics","label":"layer of (transcriptomics)"},{"from":"data-integration","to":"multi-omics","label":"method of"},{"from":"multi-omics","to":"biomarker","label":"discovers"},{"from":"multi-omics","to":"cancer-genomics","label":"applied in"},{"from":"prs","to":"genetic-risk","label":"estimates (relative)"},{"from":"genetic-risk","to":"disease-prediction","label":"input to"},{"from":"biomarker","to":"precision-medicine","label":"supports"},{"from":"disease-prediction","to":"clinical-application","label":"requires validation for"},{"from":"prs-portability","to":"ethics-equity","label":"raises"},{"from":"precision-medicine","to":"clinical-application","label":"delivered through"}],"claims":[{"id":"C-MOL-01","concept_id":"dna","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"DNA 是攜帶遺傳資訊的分子，由 A、C、G、T 四種鹼基組成；A 與 T 配對、C 與 G 配對。","en":"DNA is the molecule that carries genetic information; it uses four bases (A, C, G, T), with A pairing with T and C pairing with G."},"evidence":[{"id":"E001","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Deoxyribonucleic Acid (DNA)\" (genome.gov)","quote":"Deoxyribonucleic acid (abbreviated DNA) is the molecule that carries genetic information for the development and functioning of an organism. … Attached to each sugar is one of four bases: adenine (A), cytosine (C), guanine (G) or thymine (T). The two strands are connected by chemical bonds between the bases: adenine bonds with thymine, and cytosine bonds with guanine."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-02","concept_id":"rna","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"RNA 與 DNA 結構相似，但多為單股、骨架使用核糖（ribose），並以尿嘧啶（U）取代胸腺嘧啶（T）；細胞中有 mRNA、rRNA、tRNA 等，部分 RNA 參與基因表現調控。","en":"RNA resembles DNA but is most often single-stranded, uses ribose instead of deoxyribose, and uses uracil (U) instead of thymine (T); cells contain mRNA, rRNA and tRNA, and some RNAs regulate gene expression."},"evidence":[{"id":"E002","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Ribonucleic Acid (RNA)\" (genome.gov)","quote":"Unlike DNA, however, RNA is most often single-stranded. An RNA molecule has a backbone made of alternating phosphate groups and the sugar ribose, rather than the deoxyribose found in DNA. … Attached to each sugar is one of four bases: adenine (A), uracil (U), cytosine (C) or guanine (G). Different types of RNA exist in cells: messenger RNA (mRNA), ribosomal RNA (rRNA) and transfer RNA (tRNA). In addition, some RNAs are involved in regulating gene expression."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-03","concept_id":"chromosome","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"染色體是由蛋白質與一條 DNA 分子組成的線狀結構；人類有 22 對體染色體與 1 對性染色體，共 46 條。","en":"A chromosome is a threadlike structure of protein and a single DNA molecule; humans have 22 pairs of autosomes and one pair of sex chromosomes, 46 in total."},"evidence":[{"id":"E003","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Chromosome\" (genome.gov)","quote":"Chromosomes are threadlike structures made of protein and a single molecule of DNA that serve to carry the genomic information from cell to cell. … Humans have 22 pairs of numbered chromosomes (autosomes) and one pair of sex chromosomes (XX or XY), for a total of 46."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-04","concept_id":"gene","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"基因是遺傳的基本單位，多數基因編碼蛋白質；人類約有 20,000 個蛋白質編碼基因。","en":"The gene is the basic unit of inheritance; most genes code for proteins, and humans have approximately 20,000 protein-coding genes."},"evidence":[{"id":"E004","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Gene\" (genome.gov)","quote":"The gene is considered the basic unit of inheritance. … Most genes code for specific proteins, or segments of proteins, which have differing functions within the body. Humans have approximately 20,000 protein-coding genes."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-05","concept_id":"locus","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"Locus（基因座）是基因體中的一個實體位置，例如一個基因或其他 DNA 片段，類似街道地址；複數為 loci。","en":"A locus is a physical site in a genome, such as a gene or another DNA segment, somewhat like a street address; the plural is loci."},"evidence":[{"id":"E005","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Locus\" (genome.gov)","quote":"A locus, as related to genomics, is a physical site or location within a genome (such as a gene or another DNA segment of interest), somewhat like a street address. The plural of locus is loci."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-06","concept_id":"allele","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"Allele（對偶基因）是同一基因體位置上的不同 DNA 序列版本；每個人在該位置從父母各得一個 allele，兩者相同為同型合子（homozygous），不同為異型合子（heterozygous）。","en":"An allele is one of two or more versions of DNA sequence at a given genomic location; an individual inherits two alleles, one from each parent — identical alleles make the individual homozygous, different alleles heterozygous."},"evidence":[{"id":"E006","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Allele\" (genome.gov)","quote":"An allele is one of two or more versions of DNA sequence (a single base or a segment of bases) at a given genomic location. An individual inherits two alleles, one from each parent, for any given genomic location where such variation exists. If the two alleles are the same, the individual is homozygous for that allele. If the alleles are different, the individual is heterozygous."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-07","concept_id":"snp","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"SNP（單核苷酸多態性）是發生在單一鹼基位置的基因體變異，研究者探討 SNP 是否及如何影響健康、疾病、藥物反應與其他性狀。","en":"A single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) is a genomic variant at a single base position; scientists study if and how SNPs influence health, disease, drug response and other traits."},"evidence":[{"id":"E007","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms (SNPs)\" (genome.gov)","quote":"A single nucleotide polymorphism (abbreviated SNP, pronounced snip) is a genomic variant at a single base position in the DNA. Scientists study if and how SNPs in a genome influence health, disease, drug response and other traits."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-08","concept_id":"genetic-variant","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"1000 Genomes Project 重建了 26 個族群、2,504 人的基因體，共描述超過 8,800 萬個變異（約 8,470 萬個 SNP、360 萬個短插入/刪除與 6 萬個結構變異）。","en":"The 1000 Genomes Project reconstructed the genomes of 2,504 individuals from 26 populations and characterized over 88 million variants (84.7 million SNPs, 3.6 million short indels and 60,000 structural variants)."},"evidence":[{"id":"E008","source_id":"S06","location":"Abstract","quote":"Here we report completion of the project, having reconstructed the genomes of 2,504 individuals from 26 populations … in total over 88 million variants (84.7 million single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs), 3.6 million short insertions/deletions (indels), and 60,000 structural variants)"}]},{"id":"C-MOL-09","concept_id":"genotype","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"Genotype（基因型）是對某一基因座上變異類型的判定；部分基因型會影響個體可觀察的性狀，即 phenotype。","en":"A genotype is a scoring of the type of variant present at a given locus; some genotypes contribute to an individual's observable traits, called the phenotype."},"evidence":[{"id":"E009","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Genotype\" (genome.gov)","quote":"A genotype is a scoring of the type of variant present at a given location (i.e., a locus) in the genome. … Some genotypes contribute to an individual’s observable traits, called the phenotype."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-10","concept_id":"phenotype","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"Phenotype（表現型）是個體可觀察的性狀，例如身高、眼睛顏色與血型；它同時由基因型與環境因素決定。","en":"Phenotype refers to an individual's observable traits, such as height, eye colour and blood type, and is determined by both genotype and environmental factors."},"evidence":[{"id":"E010","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Phenotype\" (genome.gov)","quote":"Phenotype refers to an individual’s observable traits, such as height, eye color and blood type. A person’s phenotype is determined by both their genomic makeup (genotype) and environmental factors."}]},{"id":"C-MOL-11","concept_id":"genetic-variant","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"在 1000 Genomes 資料中，大多數變異位點是罕見的（約 6,400 萬個體染色體變異頻率 <0.5%）；但單一個人基因體中觀察到的變異，大多數是常見變異。","en":"In the 1000 Genomes data most variant sites are rare (~64 million autosomal variants have frequency <0.5%), yet most variants observed in a single genome are common."},"evidence":[{"id":"E066","source_id":"S06","location":"Main text, section \"A typical genome\"","quote":"The majority of variants in the data set are rare: ∼64 million autosomal variants have a frequency <0.5% … Nevertheless, the majority of variants observed in a single genome are common"}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-01","concept_id":"ngs","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"人類基因體計畫完成後，定序技術進步使每百萬鹼基成本下降、已定序基因體數量增加；有些方法追求單位時間內最多鹼基，有些則追求更長的連續讀段以解析結構複雜區域。","en":"Since the Human Genome Project, sequencing advances have lowered the cost per megabase and increased the number of sequenced genomes; some approaches maximize bases per unit time while others sequence longer contiguous DNA to resolve structurally complex regions."},"evidence":[{"id":"E011","source_id":"S03","location":"Abstract","quote":"Since the completion of the human genome project in 2003, extraordinary progress has been made in genome sequencing technologies, which has led to a decreased cost per megabase and an increase in the number and diversity of sequenced genomes. … Some approaches maximize the number of bases sequenced in the least amount of time … other approaches now aim to sequence longer contiguous pieces of DNA, which are essential for resolving structurally complex regions."}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-02","concept_id":"ngs","classification":"uncertain","text":{"zh":"（截至 2016 年）長讀段定序克服了讀段長度限制，但成本明顯較高、通量較低，限制了其普及。此描述具時效性。","en":"(As of 2016) long-read sequencing overcomes read-length limits but was considerably more expensive and lower-throughput, limiting adoption. This statement is time-sensitive."},"evidence":[{"id":"E012","source_id":"S03","location":"Main text, introduction (opening section)","quote":"Although long-read sequencing overcomes the length limitation of other NGS approaches, it remains considerably more expensive and has lower throughput than other platforms, limiting the widespread adoption of this technology in favour of less-expensive approaches."}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-03","concept_id":"wes","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"Exome（外顯子體）是基因體中所有外顯子的序列，代表蛋白質編碼部分，約占人類基因體的 1.5%。","en":"The exome is the sequence of all exons in a genome — the protein-coding portion — and is about 1.5% of the human genome."},"evidence":[{"id":"E013","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Exome\" (genome.gov)","quote":"An exome is the sequence of all the exons in a genome, reflecting the protein-coding portion of a genome. In humans, the exome is about 1.5% of the genome."}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-04","concept_id":"wgs","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"1000 Genomes Project 結合低覆蓋度全基因體定序、深度外顯子定序與高密度微陣列基因分型，說明 WGS、WES 與 array 可互補使用，而非只能擇一。","en":"The 1000 Genomes Project combined low-coverage whole-genome sequencing, deep exome sequencing and dense microarray genotyping — WGS, WES and arrays can be used together rather than only one at a time."},"evidence":[{"id":"E014","source_id":"S06","location":"Abstract","quote":"having reconstructed the genomes of 2,504 individuals from 26 populations using a combination of low-coverage whole-genome sequencing, deep exome sequencing, and dense microarray genotyping."}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-05","concept_id":"vcf","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"VCF（Variant Call Format）是儲存 SNP、插入/刪除與結構變異及其註解的通用格式，通常壓縮並建立索引以快速查詢；最初為 1000 Genomes Project 開發。","en":"The Variant Call Format (VCF) is a generic format for storing SNPs, indels and structural variants with annotations; it is usually compressed and indexed for fast retrieval and was developed for the 1000 Genomes Project."},"evidence":[{"id":"E015","source_id":"S04","location":"Abstract (Summary)","quote":"The variant call format (VCF) is a generic format for storing DNA polymorphism data such as SNPs, insertions, deletions and structural variants, together with rich annotations. VCF is usually stored in a compressed manner and can be indexed for fast data retrieval of variants from a range of positions on the reference genome. The format was developed for the 1000 Genomes Project"}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-06","concept_id":"variant-calling","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"GATK 是為 NGS 資料設計的分析框架，提供覆蓋度計算與 SNP calling 等工具，已用於 1000 Genomes Project 與 TCGA 等大型計畫。","en":"GATK is an analysis framework for next-generation sequencing data, providing tools such as coverage calculators and SNP calling, used in large projects including the 1000 Genomes Project and TCGA."},"evidence":[{"id":"E016","source_id":"S05","location":"Abstract","quote":"Here, we discuss our Genome Analysis Toolkit (GATK), a structured programming framework designed to ease the development of efficient and robust analysis tools for next-generation DNA sequencers … robust, scale-tolerant tools like coverage calculators and single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) calling. … many of which have already been incorporated into large-scale sequencing projects like the 1000 Genomes Project and The Cancer Genome Atlas."}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-07","concept_id":"mutation","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"遺傳性（germline）變異由父母傳給子女，存在於幾乎所有細胞；後天（somatic）變異在生命中某時發生，只存在部分細胞，且不會遺傳給下一代。","en":"Hereditary (germline) variants are passed from parent to child and are present in virtually every cell; acquired (somatic) variants arise during life, are present only in some cells, and cannot be passed to the next generation."},"evidence":[{"id":"E017","source_id":"S02","location":"MedlinePlus page \"What is a gene variant and how do variants occur?\"","quote":"Inherited (or hereditary) variants are passed from parent to child and are present throughout a person’s life in virtually every cell in the body. These variants are also called germline variants … Non-inherited variants occur at some time during a person’s life and are present only in certain cells, not in every cell in the body. … they are often referred to as somatic variants. These variants cannot be passed to the next generation."}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-08","concept_id":"reference-genome","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"T2T Consortium 發表完整的 30.55 億鹼基對人類基因體 T2T-CHM13，補上先前參考基因體缺少的約 8%，除 Y 染色體外所有染色體皆無缺口。","en":"The T2T Consortium presented T2T-CHM13, a complete 3.055-billion-base-pair human genome that adds the ~8% missing from earlier references, with gapless assemblies for all chromosomes except Y."},"evidence":[{"id":"E018","source_id":"S07","location":"Abstract","quote":"Addressing the remaining 8% of the genome, the Telomere-to-Telomere (T2T) Consortium presents a complete 3.055 billion-base pair sequence of a human genome, T2T-CHM13, that includes gapless assemblies for all chromosomes except Y"}]},{"id":"C-SEQ-09","concept_id":"variant-classification","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"ACMG/AMP 建議以 pathogenic、likely pathogenic、uncertain significance、likely benign、benign 五級術語描述孟德爾疾病基因中的變異，並依族群、計算、功能、共分離等證據分類。","en":"ACMG/AMP recommend five terms — pathogenic, likely pathogenic, uncertain significance, likely benign, benign — for variants in Mendelian disease genes, classified using population, computational, functional and segregation evidence."},"evidence":[{"id":"E019","source_id":"S25","location":"Abstract","quote":"This report recommends the use of specific standard terminology-\"pathogenic,\" \"likely pathogenic,\" \"uncertain significance,\" \"likely benign,\" and \"benign\"-to describe variants identified in genes that cause Mendelian disorders. Moreover, this recommendation describes a process for classifying variants into these five categories based on criteria using typical types of variant evidence (e.g., population data, computational data, functional data, segregation data)."}]},{"id":"C-TX-01","concept_id":"rna-seq","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"RNA-seq 以深度定序技術分析轉錄體；依 2009 年的回顧，它比當時的其他方法（如 microarray）能更精確測量轉錄本及其 isoform 的量。","en":"RNA-seq profiles the transcriptome with deep-sequencing technologies; a 2009 review reported that it measures transcript and isoform levels far more precisely than the other methods of that time (e.g., microarrays)."},"evidence":[{"id":"E020","source_id":"S08","location":"Abstract","quote":"RNA-Seq is a recently developed approach to transcriptome profiling that uses deep-sequencing technologies. … RNA-Seq also provides a far more precise measurement of levels of transcripts and their isoforms than other methods."}]},{"id":"C-TX-02","concept_id":"rna-seq","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"沒有一條 RNA-seq 分析流程適用所有情境；主要步驟包含實驗設計、品質控制、比對、定量、差異表現、選擇性剪接、功能分析與 eQTL mapping 等。","en":"No single RNA-seq analysis pipeline fits all cases; major steps include experimental design, quality control, alignment, quantification, differential expression, alternative splicing, functional analysis and eQTL mapping."},"evidence":[{"id":"E021","source_id":"S09","location":"Abstract","quote":"RNA-sequencing (RNA-seq) has a wide variety of applications, but no single analysis pipeline can be used in all cases. We review all of the major steps in RNA-seq data analysis, including experimental design, quality control, read alignment, quantification of gene and transcript levels, visualization, differential gene expression, alternative splicing, functional analysis, gene fusion detection and eQTL mapping."}]},{"id":"C-TX-03","concept_id":"tpm","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"Wagner 等人指出 RPKM 在不同樣本間不一致，提出修正版 TPM（transcripts per million），使樣本內平均相對莫耳濃度維持不變。","en":"Wagner et al. showed that RPKM is inconsistent among samples and proposed TPM (transcripts per million), which respects the invariance of average relative molar concentration."},"evidence":[{"id":"E022","source_id":"S10","location":"Abstract","quote":"we show that RPKM does not respect this invariance property and thus cannot be an accurate measure of rmc. We propose a slight modification of RPKM that eliminates this inconsistency and call it TPM for transcripts per million."}]},{"id":"C-TX-04","concept_id":"gene-expression","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"單看讀段數不足以比較不同樣本的表現量，因為讀段數受轉錄本長度、總讀段數與定序偏差影響，需要正規化。","en":"Read counts alone are not sufficient to compare expression among samples, because they depend on transcript length, total number of reads and sequencing biases; normalization is needed."},"evidence":[{"id":"E023","source_id":"S09","location":"Main text, section \"Transcript quantification\"","quote":"Raw read counts alone are not sufficient to compare expression levels among samples, as these values are affected by factors such as transcript length, total number of reads, and sequencing biases. The measure RPKM (reads per kilobase of exon model per million reads) [] is a within-sample normalization method"}]},{"id":"C-TX-05","concept_id":"differential-expression","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"差異表現分析面對重複數少、離散計數、動態範圍大與離群值等問題；DESeq2 以收縮估計（shrinkage）穩定 dispersion 與 fold change 的估計。","en":"Differential expression analysis faces small replicate numbers, discrete counts, large dynamic range and outliers; DESeq2 uses shrinkage estimation of dispersions and fold changes to stabilize estimates."},"evidence":[{"id":"E024","source_id":"S11","location":"Abstract","quote":"Small replicate numbers, discreteness, large dynamic range and the presence of outliers require a suitable statistical approach. We present DESeq2, a method for differential analysis of count data, using shrinkage estimation for dispersions and fold changes to improve stability and interpretability of estimates."}]},{"id":"C-TX-06","concept_id":"expression-matrix","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"差異分析的輸入是計數資料，例如 RNA-seq 中每個基因的讀段數，並比較不同實驗條件之間的系統性變化。","en":"Differential analysis takes count data — such as read counts per gene in RNA-seq — and tests for systematic changes across experimental conditions."},"evidence":[{"id":"E025","source_id":"S11","location":"Abstract","quote":"In comparative high-throughput sequencing assays, a fundamental task is the analysis of count data, such as read counts per gene in RNA-seq, for evidence of systematic changes across experimental conditions."}]},{"id":"C-TX-07","concept_id":"gene-expression","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"RNA-seq 研究已改變我們對真核生物轉錄體範圍與複雜度的認識。","en":"Studies using RNA-seq have altered our view of the extent and complexity of eukaryotic transcriptomes."},"evidence":[{"id":"E026","source_id":"S08","location":"Abstract","quote":"Studies using this method have already altered our view of the extent and complexity of eukaryotic transcriptomes."}]},{"id":"C-TX-08","concept_id":"tpm","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"相較 RPKM/FPKM，TPM 校正了轉錄本組成的差異，因此被認為在樣本間較可比。","en":"Compared with RPKM/FPKM, TPM normalizes for differences in transcript composition and is considered more comparable between samples."},"evidence":[{"id":"E067","source_id":"S09","location":"Main text, \"Transcript quantification\"","quote":"TPMs, which effectively normalize for the differences in composition of the transcripts in the denominator rather than simply dividing by the number of reads in the library, are considered more comparable between samples"}]},{"id":"C-GW-01","concept_id":"gwas","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"GWAS 在大量個體的基因體中檢測數十萬個變異，找出與特定性狀或疾病「統計上相關」的變異。","en":"GWAS test hundreds of thousands of genetic variants across many genomes to find those statistically associated with a specific trait or disease."},"evidence":[{"id":"E027","source_id":"S12","location":"Abstract","quote":"Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) test hundreds of thousands of genetic variants across many genomes to find those statistically associated with a specific trait or disease."},{"id":"E028","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Genome-Wide Association Studies (GWAS)\" (genome.gov), Definition","quote":"A genome-wide association study (abbreviated GWAS) is a research approach used to identify genomic variants that are statistically associated with a risk for a disease or a particular trait. The method involves surveying the genomes of many people, looking for genomic variants that occur more frequently in those with a specific disease or trait compared to those without the disease or trait."}]},{"id":"C-GW-02","concept_id":"gwas","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"GWAS 結果可用於理解性狀生物學、估計遺傳率、計算遺傳相關、臨床風險預測、藥物開發，以及推論風險因子與健康結果之間可能的因果關係。","en":"GWAS results are used to gain insight into a phenotype's biology, estimate heritability, calculate genetic correlations, make clinical risk predictions, inform drug development and infer potential causal relationships between risk factors and outcomes."},"evidence":[{"id":"E029","source_id":"S12","location":"Abstract","quote":"GWAS results have a range of applications, such as gaining insight into a phenotype’s underlying biology, estimating its heritability, calculating genetic correlations, making clinical risk predictions, informing drug development programmes and inferring potential causal relationships between risk factors and health outcomes."}]},{"id":"C-GW-03","concept_id":"p-value","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"GWAS 常用的全基因體顯著閾值為 p < 5 × 10⁻⁸；Visscher 等人（2017）統計約 10,000 個以此標準定義的強關聯。","en":"GWAS conventionally use a genome-wide significance threshold of p < 5 × 10⁻⁸; Visscher et al. (2017) counted about 10,000 strong associations defined this way."},"evidence":[{"id":"E030","source_id":"S13","location":"Main text, section \"General Results\" > \"Complex Traits Are Highly Polygenic\" (also Table 1)","quote":"About 10,000 strong associations have been reported between genetic variants and one or more complex traits, 10 where “strong” is defined as statistically significant at the genome-wide p value threshold of 5 × 10 −8"}]},{"id":"C-GW-04","concept_id":"ld","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"Linkage disequilibrium（LD）是不同基因座上 allele 的非隨機關聯，受重組、天擇、遺傳漂變與突變影響，被用來定位與性狀或疾病相關的基因。","en":"Linkage disequilibrium (LD) is the nonrandom association of alleles at different loci; it is shaped by recombination, selection, drift and mutation, and is used to map genes associated with traits and diseases."},"evidence":[{"id":"E031","source_id":"S14","location":"Abstract; Introduction (unheaded opening section)","quote":"Linkage disequilibrium — the nonrandom association of alleles at different loci — is a sensitive indicator of the population genetic forces that structure a genome. … how natural selection, genetic drift, recombination and mutation all affect levels of LD"}]},{"id":"C-GW-05","concept_id":"gwas","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"關聯不等於因果：GWAS 找到的顯著 SNP 通常透過 LD 標記附近未知的因果變異，之後仍需搜尋附近直接影響性狀的變異。","en":"Association is not causation: a significant GWAS SNP often tags unknown causal variants through LD, and nearby variants that directly contribute to the trait must still be searched for."},"evidence":[{"id":"E032","source_id":"S13","location":"Main text, Introduction (power and LD paragraph, before Figure 1)","quote":"The statistical power to detect associations between DNA variants and a trait depends on the experimental sample size, the distribution of effect sizes of (unknown) causal genetic variants that are segregating in the population, the frequency of those variants, and the LD between observed genotyped DNA variants and the unknown causal variants."},{"id":"E033","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Genome-Wide Association Studies (GWAS)\" (genome.gov), Definition and Narration","quote":"Once such genomic variants are identified, they are typically used to search for nearby variants that contribute directly to the disease or trait. … They inform us of correlation not causation."}]},{"id":"C-GW-06","concept_id":"effect-size","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"在二元（病例/對照）性狀中，GWAS 效應量屬於 odds ratio 尺度，通常以 log(OR) 回報；計算 PRS 時以 log(OR) 作為權重加總。","en":"For binary (case/control) phenotypes, GWAS effect sizes are on the odds-ratio scale and are typically reported as log(OR); PRS sums log(OR)-weighted genotypes."},"evidence":[{"id":"E034","source_id":"S16","location":"Main text, section 3.3 \"PRS units\"","quote":"In calculating PRS on a binary (case/control) phenotype, the effect sizes used as weights are typically reported as log Odds Ratios (log(ORs)). Assuming that relative risks on a disease accumulate on a multiplicative rather than additive scale [], then PRS should be computed as a summation of log(OR)-weighted genotypes."}]},{"id":"C-GW-07","concept_id":"gwas-catalog","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog 收錄超過 45,000 篇已發表 GWAS、5,000 多種人類性狀的變異—性狀關聯，以及超過 40,000 組完整 summary statistics（2023 年資料）。","en":"The NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog contains variant–trait associations for >45,000 published GWAS across >5,000 human traits and >40,000 full summary-statistics datasets (as of 2023)."},"evidence":[{"id":"E035","source_id":"S15","location":"Abstract","quote":"The Catalog contains variant-trait associations and supporting metadata for >45 000 published GWAS across >5000 human traits, and >40 000 full P-value summary statistics datasets."}]},{"id":"C-GW-08","concept_id":"gwas-diversity","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"2009 年分析顯示 96% 的 GWAS 參與者為歐洲血統；2016 年非歐洲比例增至近 20%，但成長多來自亞洲族群，非洲、拉丁美洲、西語裔與原住民合計仍不到 4%。","en":"A 2009 analysis found 96% of GWAS participants were of European descent; by 2016 non-European participants rose to nearly 20%, mostly from Asian populations, while African, Latin American, Hispanic and indigenous peoples together were under 4%."},"evidence":[{"id":"E036","source_id":"S24","location":"Main text, opening paragraphs and 'Persistent bias' discussion","quote":"A 2009 analysis revealed that 96% of participants in genome-wide association studies (GWAS) were of European descent … has increased to nearly 20%. Much of this rise, however, is a result of more studies being done in Asia on populations of Asian ancestry. … native or indigenous peoples represent less than 4% of all samples analysed."}]},{"id":"C-GW-09","concept_id":"manhattan-plot","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"曼哈頓圖以 x 軸表示 SNP 在基因體上的位置、y 軸表示關聯強度 −log₁₀(P)，每個點代表一個 SNP；圖中的橫線常標示全基因體顯著門檻 P < 5 × 10⁻⁸。","en":"A Manhattan plot orders SNPs on the x-axis by genomic position and shows association strength as −log10(P) on the y-axis, one dot per SNP; a horizontal line often marks the genome-wide significance threshold P < 5 × 10⁻⁸."},"evidence":[{"id":"E068","source_id":"S12","location":"Fig. 2 legend (a) (version of record, VU Research Portal)","quote":"Manhattan plot showing significance of each variant’s association with a phenotype … Each dot represents a single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP), with SNPs ordered on the x axis according to their genomic position. y axis represents strength of their association measured as –log10 transformed P values. Red line marks genome-wide significance threshold of P < 5 × 10–8."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-01","concept_id":"prs","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"PRS（多基因風險分數）是根據個體基因型與 GWAS 資料計算、估計其對某性狀或疾病遺傳傾向（genetic liability）的分數；目前的 PRS 通常只解釋性狀變異的一小部分。","en":"A polygenic risk score (PRS) estimates an individual's genetic liability to a trait or disease from their genotype profile and GWAS data; current PRSs typically explain only a small fraction of trait variance."},"evidence":[{"id":"E037","source_id":"S16","location":"Abstract","quote":"A polygenic score (PGS) or polygenic risk score (PRS) is an estimate of an individual's genetic liability to a trait or disease, calculated according to their genotype profile and relevant genome-wide association study (GWAS) data. While present PRSs typically explain only a small fraction of trait variance, their correlation with the single largest contributor to phenotypic variation-genetic liability-has led to the routine application of PRSs across biomedical research."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-02","concept_id":"prs-calculation","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"標準 PRS 是個體風險 allele 的加總，並以 GWAS 估計的效應量加權：PRS = Σ βᵢ × Gᵢ。","en":"A standard PRS is the sum of an individual's risk alleles weighted by GWAS effect size estimates: PRS = Σ βᵢ × Gᵢ."},"evidence":[{"id":"E038","source_id":"S16","location":"Introduction (opening section, before \"1 Introduction to Polygenic Risk Scores\")","quote":"In the standard approach [,–], polygenic risk scores are calculated by computing the sum of risk alleles corresponding to a phenotype of interest in each individual, weighted by the effect size estimate of the most powerful GWAS on the phenotype."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-03","concept_id":"prs-calculation","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"常見的「標準方法」是 C+T（clumping + thresholding）：以 clumping 處理 LD，再依 P 值門檻篩選 SNP。另一類方法對 summary statistics 的權重做收縮（如 LDpred，或 lassosum 這類 LASSO 型懲罰）；以個體層級基因型聯合擬合的 BLUP、LASSO 預測模型則是不同的一類。","en":"The standard approach is C+T (clumping + thresholding): LD is handled by clumping and SNPs are selected by a P-value threshold. Other methods shrink summary-statistic weights (e.g. LDpred, or LASSO-type penalties as in lassosum); BLUP or LASSO models fitted jointly on individual-level genotypes are a separate class."},"evidence":[{"id":"E039","source_id":"S16","location":"Section 3.2 \"Controlling for Linkage Disequilibrium\"; Section 3.1 \"Shrinkage of GWAS effect size estimates\"; Section 1 \"Introduction to Polygenic Risk Scores\"","quote":"phenotypic prediction approaches that exploit individual-level data only. In the latter, genotype effect sizes are typically estimated in joint models of multiple variants and prediction performed simultaneously, using approaches such as best linear unbiased prediction (BLUP) [,] or least absolute shrinkage and selection operator (LASSO) [,]. … PRS methods that perform shrinkage of all SNPs [,,,] generally exploit commonly used statistical shrinkage/regularisation techniques, such as LASSO or ridge regression … which in the case of LDpred, for example, includes a parameter for the fraction of causal variants … In the ‘standard approach’ to PRS calculation, option (1) is combined with P -value thresholding and called the C+T ( clumping + thresholding ) method, while option (2) is generally favoured in methods that implement traditional shrinkage methods"}]},{"id":"C-PRS-04","concept_id":"prs-portability","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"目前的 PRS 在歐洲血統個體中準確度高出數倍，原因是 GWAS 以歐洲族群為主；若直接用於臨床，可能擴大健康不平等。","en":"Current PRSs are several times more accurate in individuals of European ancestry because GWAS are Eurocentric; using them clinically as-is may exacerbate health disparities."},"evidence":[{"id":"E040","source_id":"S18","location":"Abstract","quote":"However, the major ethical and scientific challenge surrounding clinical implementation of PRS is that those available today are several times more accurate in individuals of European ancestry than other ancestries. This disparity is an inescapable consequence of Eurocentric biases in genome-wide association studies"},{"id":"E041","source_id":"S24","location":"Main text, opening paragraphs","quote":"A 2009 analysis revealed that 96% of participants in genome-wide association studies (GWAS) were of European descent … Our findings indicate that the proportion of individuals included in GWAS who are not of European descent has increased to nearly 20%."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-05","concept_id":"pgs-catalog","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"PGS Catalog 是公開資料庫，收錄已發表分數的變異、allele 與權重，以及可重現所需的標準化 metadata。","en":"The PGS Catalog is an open resource of published scores — variants, alleles and weights — with consistently curated metadata for reproducibility."},"evidence":[{"id":"E042","source_id":"S19","location":"Abstract","quote":"We present the Polygenic Score (PGS) Catalog (https://www.PGSCatalog.org), an open resource of published scores (including variants, alleles and weights) and consistently curated metadata required for reproducibility and independent applications."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-06","concept_id":"prs-validation","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"Khera 等人在 UK Biobank（英國血統參與者）建立並驗證五種疾病的全基因體 PRS，可找出 8.0%（冠狀動脈疾病）到 1.5%（乳癌）的人口，其勝算比（odds ratio）相較其餘人口 ≥3。","en":"Khera et al. developed and validated genome-wide PRS for five diseases in UK Biobank participants of British ancestry, identifying 8.0% (coronary artery disease) to 1.5% (breast cancer) of the population with an odds ratio ≥3 versus the remainder of the population."},"evidence":[{"id":"E043","source_id":"S20","location":"Abstract; Main text (UK Biobank study population); Online Methods \"Statistical analysis within the testing dataset\" (see also Table 2, \"Odds ratio ≥3.0\")","quote":"Here, we develop and validate genome-wide polygenic scores for five common diseases. The approach identifies 8.0, 6.1, 3.5, 3.2, and 1.5% of the population at greater than threefold increased risk for coronary artery disease, atrial fibrillation, type 2 diabetes, inflammatory bowel disease, and breast cancer, respectively. … The UK Biobank has genotype data and extensive phenotypic information on 409,258 participants of British ancestry … comparing progressively more extreme tails of the distribution to the remainder of the population in a logistic regression model"}]},{"id":"C-PRS-07","concept_id":"prs-validation","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"PRS 驗證時，base（GWAS）資料與 target 資料不能有樣本重疊，否則 PRS 與性狀的關聯會被嚴重高估。","en":"When validating a PRS, sample overlap between base (GWAS) and target data must be eliminated, because it can substantially inflate the PRS–trait association."},"evidence":[{"id":"E044","source_id":"S16","location":"Section 2 \"Quality Control of Base and Target data\", subsection \"Sample overlap\"","quote":"Sample overlap between the base and target data can result in substantial inflation of the association between the PRS and the trait tested in the target data [] and so must be eliminated."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-08","concept_id":"allele-dosage","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"在體染色體上，每人在一個位置有兩個 allele（父母各一），因此某 effect allele 的劑量（dosage）為 0、1 或 2；PRS 即加總這些 allele 並以效應量加權。","en":"On the autosomes each person carries two alleles at a location (one from each parent), so the dosage of an effect allele is 0, 1 or 2; a PRS sums these alleles weighted by effect size."},"evidence":[{"id":"E045","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Allele\" (genome.gov)","quote":"An individual inherits two alleles, one from each parent, for any given genomic location where such variation exists."},{"id":"E046","source_id":"S16","location":"Introduction (opening section, before \"1 Introduction to Polygenic Risk Scores\")","quote":"In the standard approach [,–], polygenic risk scores are calculated by computing the sum of risk alleles corresponding to a phenotype of interest in each individual, weighted by the effect size estimate of the most powerful GWAS on the phenotype."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-09","concept_id":"prs","classification":"uncertain","text":{"zh":"PRS 的個人與臨床效用仍有爭議：早期認為用 DNA 預測疾病幾乎沒有幫助，近期研究則顯示可用於找出可能受益的族群（群體層級分層）。","en":"The personal and clinical utility of PRS is debated: early work judged DNA-based prediction to add little, while recent efforts show utility for identifying groups who could benefit (group-level stratification)."},"evidence":[{"id":"E047","source_id":"S17","location":"Abstract (only abstract cached)","quote":"As a result, the practice of utilizing the DNA of an individual to predict disease has been judged to provide little to no useful information. Nevertheless, recent efforts have begun to demonstrate the utility of polygenic risk profiling to identify groups of individuals who could benefit from the knowledge of their probabilistic susceptibility to disease."}]},{"id":"C-PRS-10","concept_id":"genetic-risk","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"Khera 等人以「相較其餘人口高幾倍」（以勝算比估計）來報告高 PRS 族群的風險，並指出未來需要考慮如何同時評估絕對與相對風險，以及如何向病人溝通。","en":"Khera et al. report high-PRS groups as fold-increased risk versus the remainder of the population (estimated as odds ratios), and note that it will be important to consider how to assess both absolute and relative risks and how to communicate them."},"evidence":[{"id":"E048","source_id":"S20","location":"Abstract; Online Methods \"Statistical analysis within the testing dataset\"; Discussion (closing paragraphs of main text)","quote":"The approach identifies 8.0, 6.1, 3.5, 3.2, and 1.5% of the population at greater than threefold increased risk … Moreover, it will be important to consider how to assess both absolute and relative risks and how to communicate these risks to best serve each patient … comparing progressively more extreme tails of the distribution to the remainder of the population in a logistic regression model"}]},{"id":"C-PRS-11","concept_id":"effect-weight","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"PRS 的權重（effect weight）來自最有檢定力的 GWAS 所估計的效應量（或 Z 分數），並以 summary statistics 形式取得。","en":"PRS weights come from effect size estimates (or Z-scores) of the most powerful GWAS, obtained as summary statistics."},"evidence":[{"id":"E049","source_id":"S16","location":"Section 1 \"Introduction to Polygenic Risk Scores\"; Introduction (opening section)","quote":"weighted by the effect size estimate of the most powerful GWAS on the phenotype. … We define polygenic risk scores, or polygenic scores, as a single value estimate of an individual’s common genetic liability to a phenotype, calculated as a sum of their genome-wide genotypes, weighted by corresponding genotype effect size estimates (or Z-scores) derived from summary statistic GWAS data."}]},{"id":"C-MO-01","concept_id":"multi-omics","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"相較單一體學研究，多體學提供理解疾病背後「資訊流動」的機會；常見體學包含基因體、轉錄體、蛋白體與代謝體等。","en":"Compared with single-omics studies, multi-omics offers the opportunity to understand the flow of information underlying disease; layers include the genome, transcriptome, proteome and metabolome."},"evidence":[{"id":"E050","source_id":"S21","location":"Abstract; Introduction","quote":"As compared to studies of a single omics type, multi-omics offers the opportunity to understand the flow of information that underlies disease. … many other omics technologies have been developed that are capable of interrogation of entire pools of transcripts, proteins, and metabolites, as well as the genome (Box 1)."}]},{"id":"C-MO-02","concept_id":"data-integration","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"多體學整合可從不同起點出發：genome first 從 GWAS 位點開始探究其致病機制，phenotype first 從其他層次出發，另有 environment first；並非只有一條固定路徑。","en":"Multi-omics integration can start from different points: genome-first starts from an associated locus to find mechanisms, phenotype-first starts from another layer, and there is also environment-first — there is no single fixed path."},"evidence":[{"id":"E051","source_id":"S21","location":"Main text, section \"Approaches to integrative analysis of multiple omics data\"; Fig. 1 legend","quote":"The genome first approach implies that one starts from associated locus, while the phenotype first approach implies any other layer as the starting point. … we have grouped these into three categories, “genome first”, “phenotype first”, and “environment first”, depending on the initial focus of the investigation."}]},{"id":"C-MO-03","concept_id":"cancer-genomics","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"TCGA 在 DNA、RNA、蛋白質與表觀遺傳層次分析大量腫瘤；Pan-Cancer 計畫比較了最先完成的 12 種腫瘤類型。","en":"TCGA profiled large numbers of tumours at the DNA, RNA, protein and epigenetic levels; the Pan-Cancer initiative compared the first 12 tumour types."},"evidence":[{"id":"E052","source_id":"S22","location":"Abstract","quote":"The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) Research Network has profiled and analyzed large numbers of human tumors to discover molecular aberrations at the DNA, RNA, protein and epigenetic levels. … The Pan-Cancer initiative compares the first 12 tumor types profiled by TCGA."}]},{"id":"C-MO-04","concept_id":"biomarker","classification":"uncertain","text":{"zh":"TCGA Pan-Cancer 的目標之一，是將對某癌症有效的療法延伸到具相似基因體特徵的其他癌症（屬研究目標，非已證實結果）。","en":"One aim of TCGA Pan-Cancer is to extend therapies effective in one cancer type to others with a similar genomic profile (a research aim, not a demonstrated result)."},"evidence":[{"id":"E053","source_id":"S22","location":"Abstract","quote":"Analysis of the molecular aberrations and their functional roles across tumor types will teach us how to extend therapies effective in one cancer type to others with a similar genomic profile."}]},{"id":"C-MO-05","concept_id":"pathway-analysis","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"RNA-seq 分析常包含功能分析（例如 gene set enrichment analysis），並可與其他功能基因體技術整合。","en":"RNA-seq analysis commonly includes functional analysis (e.g. gene set enrichment analysis) and can be integrated with other functional genomics techniques."},"evidence":[{"id":"E054","source_id":"S09","location":"Abstract; section \"Functional profiling with RNA-seq\"","quote":"We discuss the analysis of small RNAs and the integration of RNA-seq with other functional genomics techniques. … gene set enrichment analysis (GSEA), which is based on ranking the transcriptome according to a measurement of differential expression."}]},{"id":"C-MO-06","concept_id":"genomics","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"基因分型晶片促成大規模 GWAS，加上全轉錄本測量方法，催生了「integrative genetics」領域；之後蛋白體學、代謝體學等其他體學也常被納入研究。","en":"Genotyping arrays enabled large-scale GWAS and, together with methods for global transcript levels, gave rise to the field of integrative genetics; other omics such as proteomics and metabolomics are now often incorporated as well."},"evidence":[{"id":"E055","source_id":"S21","location":"Abstract","quote":"The advent of genotyping arrays enabled large-scale genome-wide association studies and methods for examining global transcript levels, which gave rise to the field of \"integrative genetics\". Other omics technologies, such as proteomics and metabolomics, are now often incorporated into the everyday methodology of biological researchers."}]},{"id":"C-MO-07","concept_id":"data-integration","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"eQTL mapping 將基因型與基因表現量連結，是 RNA-seq 分析的步驟之一，也是 Mutation/變異資料與 RNA Expression 整合的典型例子。","en":"eQTL mapping links genotype to gene expression; it is one of the RNA-seq analysis steps and a typical example of integrating variant data with RNA expression."},"evidence":[{"id":"E056","source_id":"S09","location":"Main text, section \"Integration with other data types\" > \"DNA sequencing\" (eQTL mapping also listed as a step in the Abstract)","quote":"such as single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) discovery, RNA-editing analyses, or expression quantitative trait loci (eQTL) mapping. In a typical eQTL experiment, genotype and transcriptome profiles are obtained from the same tissue type across a relatively large number of individuals (>50) and correlations between genotype and expression levels are then detected."}]},{"id":"C-PM-01","concept_id":"precision-medicine","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"精準醫療是一種新興的疾病治療與預防方式，考量每個人在基因、環境與生活型態上的差異，有別於針對「平均的人」設計的一體適用策略。","en":"Precision medicine is an emerging approach to disease treatment and prevention that takes into account individual variability in genes, environment and lifestyle, unlike one-size-fits-all strategies designed for the average person."},"evidence":[{"id":"E057","source_id":"S02","location":"MedlinePlus page \"What is precision medicine?\"","quote":"According to the Precision Medicine Initiative, precision medicine is \"an emerging approach for disease treatment and prevention that takes into account individual variability in genes, environment, and lifestyle for each person.\" … It is in contrast to a one-size-fits-all approach, in which disease treatment and prevention strategies are developed for the average person, with less consideration for the differences between individuals."}]},{"id":"C-PM-02","concept_id":"precision-medicine","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"美國 Precision Medicine Initiative（2015）的近期重點是癌症，長期目標是產生適用於所有健康與疾病的知識。","en":"The US Precision Medicine Initiative (2015) had a near-term focus on cancers and a longer-term aim to generate knowledge applicable to the whole range of health and disease."},"evidence":[{"id":"E058","source_id":"S23","location":"Abstract (2015 date from article header / State of the Union, January 20, 2015)","quote":"President Obama has announced a research initiative that aims to accelerate progress toward a new era of precision medicine, with a near-term focus on cancers and a longer-term aim to generate knowledge applicable to the whole range of health and disease."}]},{"id":"C-PM-03","concept_id":"clinical-application","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"ACMG 強烈建議臨床分子遺傳檢測在 CLIA 認證實驗室進行，結果由具專科認證的臨床分子遺傳學家或同等專家判讀。","en":"ACMG strongly recommends that clinical molecular genetic testing be performed in a CLIA-approved laboratory, with results interpreted by a board-certified clinical molecular geneticist or equivalent."},"evidence":[{"id":"E059","source_id":"S25","location":"Abstract","quote":"the ACMG strongly recommends that clinical molecular genetic testing should be performed in a Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments-approved laboratory, with results interpreted by a board-certified clinical molecular geneticist or molecular genetic pathologist or the equivalent."}]},{"id":"C-PM-04","concept_id":"disease-prediction","classification":"single_study","text":{"zh":"Khera 等人主張可以開始考慮將多基因風險預測納入臨床照護；在冠狀動脈疾病中，高 PRS 族群的盛行率是具同等風險之罕見單基因突變攜帶率的 20 倍。","en":"Khera et al. proposed that it is time to contemplate including polygenic risk prediction in clinical care; for coronary artery disease, the high-PRS group was 20-fold more prevalent than carriers of rare monogenic mutations with comparable risk."},"evidence":[{"id":"E060","source_id":"S20","location":"Abstract","quote":"For coronary artery disease, this prevalence is 20-fold higher than the carrier frequency of rare monogenic mutations conferring comparable risk6. We propose that it is time to contemplate the inclusion of polygenic risk prediction in clinical care, and discuss relevant issues."}]},{"id":"C-PM-05","concept_id":"ethics-equity","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"要實現公平的 PRS 應用，遺傳研究必須優先提升族群多樣性，並公開 summary statistics，避免擴大對弱勢族群的健康不平等。","en":"To realize the equitable potential of PRS, genetic studies must prioritize diversity and publicly share summary statistics so that disparities are not increased for underserved groups."},"evidence":[{"id":"E061","source_id":"S18","location":"Abstract","quote":"To realize the full and equitable potential of PRS, greater diversity must be prioritized in genetic studies, and summary statistics must be publically disseminated to ensure that health disparities are not increased for those individuals already most underserved."},{"id":"E062","source_id":"S24","location":"Main text, section \"WHAT NOW?\"","quote":"Funding agencies should develop financial incentives for the creation of diverse cohorts of study participants. One way for them to do this would be to prioritize grant requests that propose investigations in populations of non-European (and especially of African) ancestry."}]},{"id":"C-PM-06","concept_id":"cancer-genomics","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"TCGA Pan-Cancer 計畫跨腫瘤類型比較 DNA、RNA、蛋白與表觀遺傳層次的分子異常，以建立共通性、差異與新主題的整合圖像。","en":"The TCGA Pan-Cancer project compares molecular aberrations at the DNA, RNA, protein and epigenetic levels across tumour lineages to build an integrated picture of commonalities, differences and emergent themes."},"evidence":[{"id":"E063","source_id":"S22","location":"Abstract","quote":"The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) Research Network has profiled and analyzed large numbers of human tumors to discover molecular aberrations at the DNA, RNA, protein and epigenetic levels. The resulting rich data provide a major opportunity to develop an integrated picture of commonalities, differences and emergent themes across tumor lineages."}]},{"id":"C-PM-07","concept_id":"genetic-risk","classification":"consensus","text":{"zh":"大多數常見疾病具遺傳成分，且多數疾病風險本質上是多基因的；但表現型同時受環境因素影響。","en":"Most common diseases have a genetic component and most disease risk is polygenic in nature, while phenotype is also shaped by environmental factors."},"evidence":[{"id":"E064","source_id":"S20","location":"Abstract (introductory sentences)","quote":"Because most common diseases have a genetic component, one important approach is to stratify individuals based on inherited DNA variation1. … Although most disease risk is polygenic in nature2-5, it has not yet been possible to use polygenic predictors to identify individuals at risk comparable to monogenic mutations."},{"id":"E065","source_id":"S01","location":"Glossary entry \"Phenotype\" (genome.gov)","quote":"A person’s phenotype is determined by both their genomic makeup (genotype) and environmental factors."}]}],"sources":[{"id":"S01","title":"Talking Glossary of Genomic and Genetic Terms","authors":"National Human Genome Research Institute (NHGRI), NIH","year":2026,"doi":null,"url":"https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary"},{"id":"S02","title":"MedlinePlus Genetics: Help Me Understand Genetics","authors":"U.S. National Library of Medicine, NIH","year":2026,"doi":null,"url":"https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/understanding/"},{"id":"S03","title":"Coming of age: ten years of next-generation sequencing technologies","authors":"Goodwin S, McPherson JD, McCombie WR","year":2016,"doi":"10.1038/nrg.2016.49","url":null},{"id":"S04","title":"The variant call format and VCFtools","authors":"Danecek P, Auton A, Abecasis G, et al.","year":2011,"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btr330","url":null},{"id":"S05","title":"The Genome Analysis Toolkit: a MapReduce framework for analyzing next-generation DNA sequencing data","authors":"McKenna A, Hanna M, Banks E, et al.","year":2010,"doi":"10.1101/gr.107524.110","url":null},{"id":"S06","title":"A global reference for human genetic variation","authors":"The 1000 Genomes Project Consortium","year":2015,"doi":"10.1038/nature15393","url":null},{"id":"S07","title":"The complete sequence of a human genome","authors":"Nurk S, Koren S, Rhie A, et al.","year":2022,"doi":"10.1126/science.abj6987","url":null},{"id":"S08","title":"RNA-Seq: a revolutionary tool for transcriptomics","authors":"Wang Z, Gerstein M, Snyder M","year":2009,"doi":"10.1038/nrg2484","url":null},{"id":"S09","title":"A survey of best practices for RNA-seq data analysis","authors":"Conesa A, Madrigal P, Tarazona S, et al.","year":2016,"doi":"10.1186/s13059-016-0881-8","url":null},{"id":"S10","title":"Measurement of mRNA abundance using RNA-seq data: RPKM measure is inconsistent among samples","authors":"Wagner GP, Kin K, Lynch VJ","year":2012,"doi":"10.1007/s12064-012-0162-3","url":null},{"id":"S11","title":"Moderated estimation of fold change and dispersion for RNA-seq data with DESeq2","authors":"Love MI, Huber W, Anders S","year":2014,"doi":"10.1186/s13059-014-0550-8","url":null},{"id":"S12","title":"Genome-wide association studies","authors":"Uffelmann E, Huang QQ, Munung NS, et al.","year":2021,"doi":"10.1038/s43586-021-00056-9","url":null},{"id":"S13","title":"10 Years of GWAS Discovery: Biology, Function, and Translation","authors":"Visscher PM, Wray NR, Zhang Q, et al.","year":2017,"doi":"10.1016/j.ajhg.2017.06.005","url":null},{"id":"S14","title":"Linkage disequilibrium — understanding the evolutionary past and mapping the medical future","authors":"Slatkin M","year":2008,"doi":"10.1038/nrg2361","url":null},{"id":"S15","title":"The NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog: knowledgebase and deposition resource","authors":"Sollis E, Mosaku A, Abid A, et al.","year":2023,"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkac1010","url":null},{"id":"S16","title":"Tutorial: a guide to performing polygenic risk score analyses","authors":"Choi SW, Mak TSH, O'Reilly PF","year":2020,"doi":"10.1038/s41596-020-0353-1","url":null},{"id":"S17","title":"The personal and clinical utility of polygenic risk scores","authors":"Torkamani A, Wineinger NE, Topol EJ","year":2018,"doi":"10.1038/s41576-018-0018-x","url":null},{"id":"S18","title":"Clinical use of current polygenic risk scores may exacerbate health disparities","authors":"Martin AR, Kanai M, Kamatani Y, et al.","year":2019,"doi":"10.1038/s41588-019-0379-x","url":null},{"id":"S19","title":"The Polygenic Score Catalog as an open database for reproducibility and systematic evaluation","authors":"Lambert SA, Gil L, Jupp S, et al.","year":2021,"doi":"10.1038/s41588-021-00783-5","url":null},{"id":"S20","title":"Genome-wide polygenic scores for common diseases identify individuals with risk equivalent to monogenic mutations","authors":"Khera AV, Chaffin M, Aragam KG, et al.","year":2018,"doi":"10.1038/s41588-018-0183-z","url":null},{"id":"S21","title":"Multi-omics approaches to disease","authors":"Hasin Y, Seldin M, Lusis A","year":2017,"doi":"10.1186/s13059-017-1215-1","url":null},{"id":"S22","title":"The Cancer Genome Atlas Pan-Cancer analysis project","authors":"The Cancer Genome Atlas Research Network; Weinstein JN, Collisson EA, et al.","year":2013,"doi":"10.1038/ng.2764","url":null},{"id":"S23","title":"A New Initiative on Precision Medicine","authors":"Collins FS, Varmus H","year":2015,"doi":"10.1056/NEJMp1500523","url":null},{"id":"S24","title":"Genomics is failing on diversity","authors":"Popejoy AB, Fullerton SM","year":2016,"doi":"10.1038/538161a","url":null},{"id":"S25","title":"Standards and guidelines for the interpretation of sequence variants: a joint consensus recommendation of the American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics and the Association for Molecular Pathology","authors":"Richards S, Aziz N, Bale S, et al.","year":2015,"doi":"10.1038/gim.2015.30","url":null}],"slides":[{"id":"s01","domain":"intro","title":"從 DNA 到精準醫療","subtitle":"From DNA to Precision Medicine — 基因體學、轉錄體學、GWAS 與 PRS 互動教學","beginner":["這份簡報帶你從一個 DNA 字母，一路走到「為什麼同一種病，不同人需要不同照護」。","每一章都有 <b>Beginner</b> 與 <b>Advanced</b> 兩種講法，右上角可以切換。","每頁下方的「來源追溯」可以點到 Wiki 條目、證據紀錄與原始文獻。"],"advanced":["範圍：Molecular Biology、Sequencing &amp; Variant Analysis、Transcriptomics、GWAS、PRS、Multi-Omics、Precision Medicine。","每個科學主張都對應 <code>evidence/claims.json</code> 中的 Claim ID，並標示 Consensus / Single Study Finding / Uncertain。","本教材<b>非臨床診斷工具</b>；PRS 計算器只使用模擬資料（simulated data, not real patients）。"],"visual":"title","concept_ids":[],"claim_ids":[]},{"id":"s02","domain":"intro","title":"地圖：不同方法回答不同問題","beginner":["WGS、RNA-seq、GWAS、PRS、Multi-Omics 是一組<b>工具箱</b>，不是一條每項研究都要依序走完的單一流程。","先問「我想知道什麼？」再選工具：想找變異 → 定序；想看基因忙不忙 → RNA-seq；想找和疾病相關的位置 → GWAS。"],"advanced":["研究設計決定資料：例如 GWAS 常用基因分型晶片 + imputation，而非 WGS；RNA-seq 也不需要先做 WGS。","Multi-Omics 的整合可以從 genome、phenotype 或 environment 任一層出發（C-MO-02），並非固定路徑。"],"visual":"toolbox","concept_ids":["multi-omics","data-integration"],"claim_ids":["C-MO-02","C-SEQ-04"]},{"id":"s03","domain":"molecular","title":"DNA 與染色體","beginner":["DNA 用四個字母 <b>A、C、G、T</b> 寫成，兩股像拉鍊一樣扣住：A 對 T、C 對 G。","DNA 很長，被包裝成一條條<b>染色體（Chromosome）</b>。人類有 23 對、共 46 條：一半來自媽媽、一半來自爸爸。"],"advanced":["DNA：去氧核糖–磷酸骨架 + 四種鹼基，反向平行雙股互補配對。","Chromosome：一條連續 DNA 分子 + 蛋白質；22 對 autosome + 1 對性染色體（XX/XY）。基因體座標寫作 <code>chr:position</code>。"],"visual":"helix","concept_ids":["dna","chromosome"],"claim_ids":["C-MOL-01","C-MOL-03"]},{"id":"s04","domain":"molecular","title":"Gene 與 Locus：內容 vs. 地址","beginner":["<b>Gene（基因）</b>是說明書中的一個章節，多數負責製造蛋白質；人類約有 2 萬個蛋白質編碼基因。","<b>Locus（基因座）</b>是「地址」：在哪條染色體的哪個位置。Gene 是內容，Locus 是位置。"],"advanced":["Gene 是遺傳的基本單位，包含外顯子、內含子與調控序列。","Locus 可以是單一鹼基或一段區域；GWAS 的 risk locus 是關聯區域，不一定等於單一基因。"],"visual":"gene-locus","concept_ids":["gene","locus"],"claim_ids":["C-MOL-04","C-MOL-05"]},{"id":"s05","domain":"molecular","title":"DNA Explorer：Allele、SNP 與 Genotype","beginner":["點選下方的 SNP 位置，替兩條染色體（父／母）選擇不同的 <b>allele</b>，看看 genotype 怎麼變。","SNP 是只差<b>一個字母</b>的地方。每人在每個位置有兩份 allele。"],"advanced":["Allele 相同為 homozygous、不同為 heterozygous；以 effect allele 計數即得 dosage 0/1/2，這就是 PRS 的 Gᵢ。","注意：本頁序列與 SNP 皆為<b>模擬示例</b>。"],"widget":"dna-explorer","concept_ids":["allele","snp","genotype","allele-dosage"],"claim_ids":["C-MOL-06","C-MOL-07","C-PRS-08"]},{"id":"s06","domain":"molecular","title":"Genotype ≠ Phenotype","beginner":["<b>Genotype（基因型）</b>是寫在 DNA 裡的版本組合；<b>Phenotype（表現型）</b>是看得到、量得到的特徵，例如身高、血型、是否罹病。","Phenotype 同時受基因和環境（飲食、運動、生活）影響，所以基因不是命運。"],"advanced":["Genotype：某 locus 的變異判定（硬判定 0/1/2 或 imputed dosage）。","Phenotype 可為連續性狀（用 β）或二元性狀（用 OR），決定 GWAS 的迴歸模型。","1000 Genomes Project 在 26 族群 2,504 人中描述 >8,800 萬個變異——人類變異普遍：多數變異位點罕見，但每個人身上的變異多數是常見變異。"],"visual":"geno-pheno","concept_ids":["genotype","phenotype","genetic-variant"],"claim_ids":["C-MOL-09","C-MOL-10","C-MOL-08"]},{"id":"s07","domain":"sequencing","title":"次世代定序 NGS","beginner":["NGS 把 DNA 剪成數百萬段小片段同時讀取，再用電腦拼回來。","定序成本大幅下降，讓我們能讀更多人的基因體。"],"advanced":["短讀段：高通量、低成本；長讀段：能跨越重複序列與結構變異。","<span class=\"tag-uncertain\">Uncertain（具時效性）</span>：2016 年時長讀段成本較高、通量較低；此情況已在改變。","所有讀段都要對照<b>參考基因體</b>；T2T-CHM13（2022）補上舊參考缺少的約 8%。"],"visual":"reads","concept_ids":["ngs","reference-genome"],"claim_ids":["C-SEQ-01","C-SEQ-02","C-SEQ-08"]},{"id":"s08","domain":"sequencing","title":"WGS vs. WES","beginner":["<b>WGS</b>：整本說明書從頭讀到尾。","<b>WES</b>：只讀外顯子（exome，製造蛋白質的段落），約占基因體 1.5%，比較便宜，但會漏掉其他區域的變異。"],"advanced":["WGS 覆蓋編碼與非編碼區、結構變異偵測較佳；WES 以探針捕捉外顯子，覆蓋度較不均勻。","兩者可以互補：1000 Genomes 同時使用低覆蓋 WGS、深度 WES 與晶片。"],"visual":"wgs-wes","concept_ids":["wgs","wes"],"claim_ids":["C-SEQ-03","C-SEQ-04"]},{"id":"s09","domain":"sequencing","title":"Variant Calling 與 VCF","beginner":["把讀段對回參考基因體，逐一檢查每個位置是否不同——這就是 <b>Variant Calling</b>。","結果存成 <b>VCF</b> 表格：哪條染色體、哪個位置、原本是什麼、變成什麼、每個人的基因型。"],"advanced":["流程：alignment → duplicate marking → base-quality recalibration → genotype calling → filtering（GATK 為代表框架）。","VCF 欄位：<code>CHROM POS ID REF ALT QUAL FILTER INFO FORMAT</code> + 樣本欄；常以 bgzip + tabix 壓縮索引。"],"visual":"vcf","concept_ids":["variant-calling","vcf"],"claim_ids":["C-SEQ-05","C-SEQ-06"]},{"id":"s10","domain":"sequencing","title":"Germline vs. Somatic Mutation","beginner":["<b>Germline</b>：從父母遺傳，幾乎每個細胞都有，可能傳給下一代。","<b>Somatic</b>：出生後才在部分細胞發生（例如癌細胞），不會遺傳給孩子。"],"advanced":["Germline 變異是 GWAS/PRS 的基礎；somatic 變異是癌症基因體重點，常用腫瘤–正常配對樣本偵測。","孟德爾疾病變異以 ACMG/AMP 五級分類：Pathogenic、Likely pathogenic、VUS、Likely benign、Benign。"],"visual":"germ-soma","concept_ids":["mutation","variant-classification"],"claim_ids":["C-SEQ-07","C-SEQ-09"]},{"id":"s11","domain":"transcriptomics","title":"DNA 是食譜，RNA 是正在煮的菜","beginner":["每個細胞有同一本 DNA 說明書，但肝細胞和腦細胞「翻開來用」的章節不同。","<b>Mutation（突變）</b>是 DNA 字母改了；<b>Gene Expression（基因表現）</b>是 RNA 的量變多或變少。兩件事不同！"],"advanced":["RNA 多為單股、使用 U 取代 T；mRNA 豐度常被用來近似基因表現量。","Mutation 屬基因體層次（DNA 序列）；expression 屬轉錄體層次（RNA 豐度），會隨組織、時間與狀態改變。"],"visual":"dogma","concept_ids":["rna","gene-expression","mutation"],"claim_ids":["C-MOL-02","C-TX-07"]},{"id":"s12","domain":"transcriptomics","title":"RNA-seq 在做什麼？","beginner":["把細胞裡的 RNA 抓出來定序，數一數每個基因的「影印本」有幾份。","結果整理成一張大表：每列一個基因、每欄一個樣本（Gene Expression Matrix）。"],"advanced":["依 2009 年回顧，RNA-seq 比當時的方法（如 microarray）更精確地測量轉錄本與 isoform 的量。","主要步驟：design → QC → alignment → quantification → DE / splicing / functional analysis / eQTL。<b>沒有一條流程適用所有研究</b>。"],"visual":"matrix","concept_ids":["rna-seq","expression-matrix"],"claim_ids":["C-TX-01","C-TX-02","C-TX-06"]},{"id":"s13","domain":"transcriptomics","title":"TPM：長度與深度的校正","beginner":["長的基因天生會被讀到比較多次，所以不能直接比讀段數。","TPM 先除以基因長度，再換算成「每一百萬個轉錄本中占幾個」。下方用模擬數字示範。"],"advanced":["TPMᵢ = (cᵢ/ℓᵢ) / Σⱼ(cⱼ/ℓⱼ) × 10⁶；每個樣本 TPM 總和固定為 10⁶（Wagner 2012 對 RPKM 不一致性的修正）。","<b>限制</b>：TPM 是相對量；差異表現檢定應使用 count 模型（如 DESeq2），而非直接比較 TPM。見文獻衝突 CF-02。"],"visual":"tpm","concept_ids":["tpm","gene-expression"],"claim_ids":["C-TX-03","C-TX-04"]},{"id":"s14","domain":"transcriptomics","title":"Differential Expression","beginner":["比較兩組（例如病人 vs. 健康者），找出表現量明顯不同的基因。","需要多個重複樣本，才能分辨「真的不同」與「隨機波動」。"],"advanced":["DESeq2：Kᵢⱼ ~ NB(μᵢⱼ, αᵢ)，以 shrinkage 穩定 dispersion 與 log₂ fold change，處理重複數少、離散計數與離群值。","結果常以 log₂FC 與 FDR 校正後的 p 值呈現。"],"visual":"volcano","concept_ids":["differential-expression","expression-matrix"],"claim_ids":["C-TX-05","C-TX-06"]},{"id":"s15","domain":"gwas","title":"GWAS：在整個基因體找關聯","beginner":["比較「有病」和「沒病」的一大群人，看哪些 SNP 在病人中比較常見。","找到的是<b>關聯</b>，不是證明那個 SNP 就是病因——<b>關聯不等於因果</b>。"],"advanced":["對每個 SNP 迴歸 phenotype ~ dosage + covariates（含主成分以校正族群分層）。","GWAS 結果可用於生物機制、遺傳率、遺傳相關、風險預測、藥物開發與因果推論。"],"visual":"case-control","concept_ids":["gwas","snp","phenotype"],"claim_ids":["C-GW-01","C-GW-02"]},{"id":"s16","domain":"gwas","title":"P-value 與全基因體顯著","beginner":["一次檢查上百萬個 SNP，很容易碰巧「中獎」，所以門檻很嚴格：<b>p &lt; 5 × 10⁻⁸</b>。","下方是<b>模擬</b>的 GWAS 結果圖：高過虛線的點才算全基因體顯著。"],"advanced":["5 × 10⁻⁸ ≈ 0.05 / 10⁶，約等於對一百萬個獨立檢定做 Bonferroni 校正。","P 值小 = 統計證據強，不代表效應大，也不代表因果。","Manhattan plot：x 軸為基因體位置、y 軸為 −log₁₀(P)，每點一個 SNP（Uffelmann 2021 Fig. 2）；本頁圖為自製模擬圖。"],"visual":"manhattan","concept_ids":["p-value","manhattan-plot"],"claim_ids":["C-GW-03","C-GW-09"]},{"id":"s17","domain":"gwas","title":"LD：為什麼關聯不等於因果","beginner":["距離很近的 SNP 常常「一起被遺傳」，像同一節車廂的乘客。","所以 GWAS 找到的 SNP 可能只是「乘客」，真正的病因在同一節車廂的別人身上。"],"advanced":["LD：不同基因座 allele 的非隨機關聯；r² = D² / [p_A(1−p_A)p_B(1−p_B)]。","顯著 SNP 常透過 LD 標記未知的因果變異，需要 fine-mapping 與功能研究。LD 結構因族群而異。"],"visual":"ld","concept_ids":["ld","gwas"],"claim_ids":["C-GW-04","C-GW-05"]},{"id":"s18","domain":"gwas","title":"Effect Size 與研究族群","beginner":["效應量回答「影響有多大」：連續性狀用 <b>β</b>，疾病用 <b>Odds Ratio</b>。","過去大多數 GWAS 參與者是歐洲血統，結果用在其他族群不一定一樣準。"],"advanced":["二元性狀：OR = e^β，β = log(OR)；交換 effect allele 時 β 變號。","2009 年 96% GWAS 參與者為歐洲血統；2016 年非歐洲約 20%，但非洲、拉丁美洲血統、西語裔與原住民合計 &lt;4%。","GWAS Catalog 收錄 >45,000 篇 GWAS 的關聯（2023 年）。"],"visual":"ancestry","concept_ids":["effect-size","gwas-diversity","gwas-catalog"],"claim_ids":["C-GW-06","C-GW-08","C-GW-07"]},{"id":"s19","domain":"prs","title":"PRS：很多小影響加起來","beginner":["很多疾病不是單一基因造成，而是成千上萬個小影響累加。","PRS 把這些影響加權加總成一個分數，用來和其他人比<b>相對高低</b>，不是「會不會得病」的答案。"],"advanced":["PRS 估計 genetic liability，通常只解釋性狀變異的一小部分。","<span class=\"tag-uncertain\">Uncertain</span>：個人與臨床效用仍有爭議；目前證據主要支持群體層級分層（見 CF-01）。"],"visual":"many-small","concept_ids":["prs"],"claim_ids":["C-PRS-01","C-PRS-09"]},{"id":"s20","domain":"prs","title":"公式：PRS = Σ(βᵢ × Gᵢ)","beginner":["<b>βᵢ</b>：第 i 個 SNP 的權重（來自 GWAS 效應量）。","<b>Gᵢ</b>：你有幾個 effect allele（0、1 或 2）。","每個 SNP「權重 × 個數」，全部加起來就是 PRS。"],"advanced":["權重取自 GWAS summary statistics 的 β 或 log(OR)；二元性狀常用 log(OR)。","標準方法 C+T：clumping 處理 LD + P 值門檻；LDpred、lassosum 等收縮 summary statistics 權重；以個體層級資料聯合擬合的 BLUP / LASSO 是另一類。","Imputed dosage 可為 0–2 間的小數，例如 1.4。"],"visual":"formula","concept_ids":["prs-calculation","effect-weight","allele-dosage","effect-allele"],"claim_ids":["C-PRS-02","C-PRS-03","C-PRS-11","C-GW-06"]},{"id":"s21","domain":"prs","title":"PRS Calculator（模擬資料）","beginner":["調整每個 SNP 的 dosage（0、1、2）與權重 β，看看分數和每個 SNP 的貢獻怎麼變。","⚠️ 所有 SNP 與權重都是<b>模擬資料</b>，不是任何真實患者或真實 GWAS 結果。"],"advanced":["計算核心 <code>assets/js/prs.js</code> 經 Python 參考實作與 node 單元測試驗證（含負權重、小數 dosage、多 SNP 加總）。","原始 PRS 的單位沒有臨床意義；實務上需在參考族群中標準化（z-score / 百分位）並評估其表現。"],"widget":"prs-calculator","concept_ids":["prs-calculation","allele-dosage","effect-weight"],"claim_ids":["C-PRS-02","C-PRS-08"]},{"id":"s22","domain":"prs","title":"驗證、族群適用性與「相對 vs. 絕對」","beginner":["分數要拿到<b>沒看過的新一群人</b>測試；用同一群人自己考自己會高估。","主要用歐洲族群資料做出的分數，用在其他族群常常不夠準。","「風險高 1.5 倍」：如果原本是 2%，變成約 3%——<b>相對風險 ≠ 絕對風險</b>。"],"advanced":["Base 與 target 樣本不可重疊，否則嚴重高估關聯。","目前 PRS 在歐洲血統中準確度高出數倍（Martin 2019）。","Khera 2018 報告高 PRS 族群相較其餘人口的勝算比 ≥3（結果罕見時約等於相對風險），並指出需考慮如何同時評估與溝通絕對與相對風險；其樣本為英國血統單一世代。"],"visual":"abs-rel","concept_ids":["prs-validation","prs-portability","genetic-risk"],"claim_ids":["C-PRS-07","C-PRS-04","C-PRS-06","C-PRS-10"]},{"id":"s23","domain":"multiomics","title":"Multi-Omics：同時看好幾層","beginner":["只看 DNA 像只看食譜；只看 RNA 像只看正在煮什麼。多體學把好幾層一起看。","常見層次：Genomics（DNA）、Transcriptomics（RNA）、Proteomics（蛋白質）、Metabolomics（代謝物）。"],"advanced":["相較單一體學，多體學有機會理解疾病背後的資訊流動。","基因分型晶片促成大規模 GWAS，加上全轉錄本測量，催生 integrative genetics；之後其他體學也常被納入。"],"visual":"layers","concept_ids":["multi-omics","genomics"],"claim_ids":["C-MO-01","C-MO-06"]},{"id":"s24","domain":"multiomics","title":"Mutation × RNA Expression 的整合","beginner":["把 DNA 變異和 RNA 表現放在一起看：某個變異會不會讓附近基因表現變高或變低？","下方<b>模擬</b>圖：不同 genotype 的人，某基因的表現量分布。"],"advanced":["eQTL mapping：expression ~ dosage，連結基因體與轉錄體層次。","整合策略可為 genome first、phenotype first、environment first——<b>並非單一固定路徑</b>。","挑戰：樣本對應、批次效應、資料尺度差異與缺失值。"],"visual":"eqtl","concept_ids":["data-integration","multi-omics"],"claim_ids":["C-MO-07","C-MO-02"]},{"id":"s25","domain":"multiomics","title":"Pathway 與 Biomarker","beginner":["幾百個差異基因很難懂；<b>Pathway Analysis</b> 問：它們是否集中在某些生物功能？","<b>Biomarker</b> 是可測量、能反映身體狀態的指標，例如某個突變或表現特徵。"],"advanced":["功能分析（如 GSEA）是 RNA-seq 常見步驟，並可與其他功能基因體技術整合。","<span class=\"tag-uncertain\">Uncertain</span>：TCGA Pan-Cancer 的目標之一是依基因體特徵跨癌種延伸療法——這是研究目標，非已證實結果。"],"visual":"pathway","concept_ids":["pathway-analysis","biomarker"],"claim_ids":["C-MO-05","C-MO-04"]},{"id":"s26","domain":"precision","title":"精準醫療是什麼？","beginner":["傳統醫療常為「平均的病人」設計；精準醫療考慮每個人的<b>基因、環境與生活型態</b>。","基因只是其中一塊拼圖。"],"advanced":["定義：考量個體在基因、環境、生活型態差異的疾病治療與預防方式。","美國 Precision Medicine Initiative（2015）近期聚焦癌症，長期擴及所有健康與疾病。","大多數常見疾病具遺傳成分且多為多基因，但表現型同時受環境影響。"],"visual":"puzzle","concept_ids":["precision-medicine","genetic-risk"],"claim_ids":["C-PM-01","C-PM-02","C-PM-07"]},{"id":"s27","domain":"precision","title":"癌症基因體與臨床應用","beginner":["癌症來自細胞 DNA 的後天（somatic）變化。分析腫瘤的 DNA、RNA 等資料，可以幫助分類並尋找治療方向。","研究發現要用在病人身上，需要合格實驗室與專業判讀。"],"advanced":["TCGA 在 DNA、RNA、蛋白質與表觀層次分析大量腫瘤；Pan-Cancer 比較 12 種腫瘤類型。","ACMG 建議臨床分子遺傳檢測在 CLIA 認證實驗室進行，由認證專家判讀。"],"visual":"tumor","concept_ids":["cancer-genomics","clinical-application"],"claim_ids":["C-MO-03","C-PM-06","C-PM-03"]},{"id":"s28","domain":"precision","title":"預測、公平與倫理：兩種觀點並陳","beginner":["有研究主張可以開始考慮把 PRS 用在臨床；也有研究提醒：分數對不同族群準確度不同，可能擴大不公平。","我們把兩種觀點都列出來，而不是只挑一個結論。"],"advanced":["Khera 2018（single study，英國血統 UK Biobank）：主張考慮將多基因風險預測納入臨床。","Martin 2019：目前 PRS 在歐洲血統準確數倍，需提升多樣性並公開 summary statistics。","PRS 引導篩檢能否改善臨床結果：本系統<b>尚無可驗證證據</b>（C-PRS-12 Pending）。"],"visual":"two-views","concept_ids":["disease-prediction","ethics-equity","prs-portability"],"claim_ids":["C-PM-04","C-PM-05","C-PRS-04"]},{"id":"s29","domain":"review","title":"互動測驗","beginner":["每題選一個答案，會立即顯示正確與否以及理由，並連到相關 Wiki 條目。"],"advanced":["題目涵蓋七大領域；理由引用本系統已驗證的主張。"],"widget":"quiz","concept_ids":[],"claim_ids":[]},{"id":"s30","domain":"review","title":"總結與這份教材是怎麼做出來的","beginner":["DNA、變異、表現、關聯、分數、整合、照護是不同層次的問題與工具，可依研究問題單獨或組合使用，各有用途與限制。","記住三件事：<b>關聯不等於因果</b>、<b>PRS 是相對而非絕對風險</b>、<b>族群差異很重要</b>。"],"advanced":["本教材由 8 節點 Graph / Loop 流程產生：Source Ingestion → Evidence Validation → Wiki → Quality Gate → Slides → HTML &amp; Scientific Validation → Independent AI Review → Publish。","25 份來源經 Crossref / HTTP 驗證；每條主張可追溯；證據不足的主張停止發布。"],"visual":"workflow","concept_ids":["precision-medicine","gwas","prs"],"claim_ids":["C-GW-05","C-PRS-10","C-PRS-04"]}],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","domain":"molecular","concept_id":"locus","q":"「Gene」和「Locus」的差別，哪個說法最正確？","options":["兩者是同義詞","Gene 是遺傳的功能單位（內容），Locus 是基因體中的位置（地址）","Locus 一定比 Gene 長","Locus 只存在於性染色體"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Locus 是基因體中的實體位置，類似街道地址；Gene 是遺傳的基本單位，多數編碼蛋白質（C-MOL-04、C-MOL-05）。"},{"id":"q2","domain":"molecular","concept_id":"phenotype","q":"下列哪一項是 Phenotype（表現型）？","options":["某 SNP 的基因型 A/G","血型","VCF 中的 0/1","rsID 編號"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Phenotype 是可觀察的性狀，例如身高、眼睛顏色與血型；它由基因型與環境共同決定（C-MOL-10）。"},{"id":"q3","domain":"sequencing","concept_id":"mutation","q":"只在腫瘤細胞中出現、同一人血液 DNA 中沒有的變異，最可能是？","options":["Germline variant","Somatic variant","Reference allele","eQTL"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Somatic（後天）變異只存在部分細胞，且不會遺傳給下一代（C-SEQ-07）。"},{"id":"q4","domain":"sequencing","concept_id":"wes","q":"WES（全外顯子定序）大約涵蓋人類基因體的多少？","options":["約 1.5%","約 25%","約 50%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Exome 是所有外顯子的序列，約占人類基因體的 1.5%（C-SEQ-03）。"},{"id":"q5","domain":"transcriptomics","concept_id":"tpm","q":"為什麼不能直接用讀段數比較兩個樣本的基因表現？","options":["因為讀段數一定是 0","因為讀段數受轉錄本長度、總讀段數與定序偏差影響","因為 RNA 沒有序列","因為 TPM 是 DNA 的單位"],"answer":1,"explanation":"讀段數受轉錄本長度、定序深度與偏差影響，需要正規化（C-TX-04）。"},{"id":"q6","domain":"transcriptomics","concept_id":"gene-expression","q":"Mutation 與 Gene Expression 的差別是？","options":["沒有差別","Mutation 是 DNA 序列改變；Gene Expression 是 RNA 豐度","Mutation 是 RNA 量變多","Gene Expression 只發生在癌症"],"answer":1,"explanation":"突變屬基因體層次；基因表現屬轉錄體層次，以 RNA 量近似（C-SEQ-07、C-TX-04）。"},{"id":"q7","domain":"gwas","concept_id":"gwas","q":"GWAS 找到某 SNP 與疾病顯著相關（p < 5×10⁻⁸），最恰當的解讀是？","options":["這個 SNP 就是病因","此 SNP 與疾病統計上相關，可能透過 LD 標記附近的因果變異","帶這個 SNP 的人一定會得病","效應一定很大"],"answer":1,"explanation":"關聯不等於因果；顯著 SNP 常透過 LD 標記附近未知的因果變異（C-GW-05）。"},{"id":"q8","domain":"prs","concept_id":"prs-calculation","q":"（模擬）β = (0.2, −0.1)，dosage = (2, 2)。PRS = ？","options":["0.6","0.2","0.1","−0.2"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PRS = Σβᵢ×Gᵢ = 0.2×2 + (−0.1)×2 = 0.4 − 0.2 = 0.2（C-PRS-02）。"},{"id":"q9","domain":"prs","concept_id":"genetic-risk","q":"某人 PRS 屬於「相較其餘人口勝算比 ≥3」的群體，代表什麼？","options":["此人有 300% 機率得病","此人一定會得病","相對於其他人口風險較高，絕對風險還取決於比較組的發生率","此人不需要任何篩檢"],"answer":2,"explanation":"這是相對比較（Khera 2018 以勝算比報告）；絕對風險還要結合比較組的發生率，研究者也指出需考慮如何同時溝通兩者（C-PRS-10）。"},{"id":"q10","domain":"prs","concept_id":"prs-portability","q":"以歐洲血統 GWAS 建立的 PRS，用於非洲血統族群時通常會？","options":["準確度相同","準確度較低","準確度一定更高","無法計算"],"answer":1,"explanation":"目前 PRS 在歐洲血統中準確度高出數倍，源於 GWAS 的歐洲偏重（C-PRS-04）。"},{"id":"q11","domain":"multiomics","concept_id":"data-integration","q":"關於多體學整合，哪個說法正確？","options":["必須先做 WGS，再做 RNA-seq，最後才能做 GWAS","可以從 genome、phenotype 或 environment 任一層出發","只能分析單一體學","多體學等於 PRS"],"answer":1,"explanation":"整合策略包括 genome first、phenotype first 與 environment first，並非單一固定路徑（C-MO-02）。"},{"id":"q12","domain":"precision","concept_id":"precision-medicine","q":"精準醫療考量的個體差異包括？","options":["只有基因","基因、環境與生活型態","只有年齡","只有 PRS"],"answer":1,"explanation":"精準醫療考慮個體在基因、環境與生活型態上的差異（C-PM-01）。"}]};
